\v 12 \add ≈Their¦337577 leader¦337574\add* will¦337581 lift¦337581 his things up¦337581 onto his shoulder¦337580 in¦337577 the dark¦337582, and¦337583 will¦337583 go¦337583 out¦337583 through the wall¦337584. They'll dig¦337585 through the wall and take¦337586 their¦337577 things out. He'll¦337581 cover¦337589 his face¦337588, so he¦337589 won't¦337592 see¦337594 the¦337600 \add ≈place\add* \add he's leaving\add*.
\v 13 I'll spread¦337602 my net¦337605 out over him and¦337607 he'll be¦337607 caught¦337607 in¦337608 my trap, then¦337602 I'll take¦337609 him¦337610 \add away\add* to¦337611 Babylon¦337611 (the¦337612 land¦337612 of¦337612 the¦337613 Chaldeans¦337613), but¦337602 he¦337607 won't¦337615 see¦337617 it¦337606, and he'll die¦337619 there¦337618.\x + \xo 12:13: \xt 2Ki 25:7; Jer 52:11.\x*
\v 14 I'll also¦337626 scatter¦337629 all¦337621 of¦337623 his assistants¦337624 in every¦337630 direction, and¦337621 I'll send out a sword¦337633 after¦337635 his entire¦337626 army.
\v 15 When¦337637 I scatter¦337645 them among¦337644 the nations¦337644 and¦337645 disperse¦337642 them throughout the lands¦337647, then¦337637 they'll¦337637 know¦337637 that¦337638 I am¦337641 Yahweh¦337641.
