\p Haven't you¦339600 added prostitution to¦339608 all¦339609 your¦339632 other detestable¦339632 practices?
\v 44 Listen, everyone¦339635 who¦339637 speaks¦339639 proverbs¦339637 about¦339638 you¦339638 will¦339639 say¦339640, “Like¦339641 mother¦339641, like¦339641 daughter¦339642.”
\v 45 You¦339647 are the daughter¦339644 of¦339644 your mother¦339646, who¦339648 detested her¦339649 husband¦339649 and¦339650 her children, and¦339651 you¦339653 are the sister¦339651 of¦339651 your¦339652 sisters¦339652, who¦339654 detested their husbands¦339656 and their children. Your¦339646 mother¦339658 was¦339659 a Hittite¦339659, and¦339660 your father¦339660 was¦339661 an¦339661 Amorite¦339661.
\p
\v 46 Your¦339671 older¦339664 sister was¦339665 Shomron¦339665 \add !(Samaria¦339665)\add*, and¦339667 her¦339667 daughters¦339667 were the ones living in the north¦339671, while your¦339671 younger¦339673 sister was the one living south¦339676 of¦339676 you¦339674, that¦339675 is¦339677, Sodom¦339677 and¦339678 her daughters.
\v 47 \add ≈Not¦339680 only¦339687 did you follow\add* their customs and copy their behaviour¦339688 and practices, but¦339680 in¦339681 \add ≈everything you¦339682 did¦339684\add*, you've been \em worse\em* than¦339689 they were.
\p
\v 48 This is the¦339694 master¦339698 Yahweh's¦339699 declaration¦339697: As¦339707 I live¦339694, your sister¦339704 Sodom¦339703 and¦339706 her¦339706 daughters¦339706 didn't do as much evil as you¦339708 and your daughters have¦339708 done¦339708.
\v 49 Listen, your¦339718 sister¦339718 Sodom's¦339717 sin was that¦339714 she¦339733 was arrogant in her¦339727 leisure, careless and unconcerned about¦339716 anything. She¦339733 didn't¦339732 \add ≈assist\add* the¦339728 poor¦339730 and¦339731 needy¦339731 people.
\v 50 She¦339742 was¦339735 arrogant and¦339735 performed¦339736 disgusting actions \add ≈in front¦339738 of\add* me¦339738, so I¦339739 took¦339739 them¦339740 away, just¦339741 as¦339741 you've seen¦339742.
\p
\v 51 As for Shomron¦339745, they didn't¦339748 commit even half¦339746 of¦339746 your sins¦339747. No, you've done¦339764 many¦339760 more¦339754 disgusting things than¦339754 they did¦339755, and¦339755 you've shown that¦339763 your sisters¦339758 were better than you, because of¦339758 all¦339760 the¦339746 disgusting things you do¦339764.
\v 52 Also¦339767 how you¦339769 display your¦339772 own shame—you've¦339774 shown that¦339777 your sisters were better than you by¦339776 the sins¦339776 you committed in¦339776 all those¦339780 disgusting ways. Your¦339788 sisters now seem better than you.
\rem /s1 Sodom and Samaria Will Be Restored
\p
\v 53 From their¦339795 captivity¦339810, I'll¦339792 restore¦339792 the¦339798 fortunes of Sodom¦339800 and¦339801 her¦339801 daughters¦339801, and¦339802 of Shomron¦339806 and¦339807 her¦339807 daughters¦339807, and¦339808 your¦339810 fortunes \add ≈will¦339792 be similar\add*,\f + \fr 16:53 \ft i.e., to go into captivity, but then after a time, to be restored.\f*
\v 54 so¦339813 that¦339813 you'll display your¦339815 shame¦339815. You'll be¦339816 humiliated¦339816 because of¦339815 everything you've¦339820 done¦339820, and¦339816 in¦339821 that way you'll be a consolation¦339821 to \add @Sodom¦339822 and¦339822 Shomron¦339822\add*.
\v 55 Your¦339824 sister¦339824 Sodom¦339825 and¦339826 her¦339826 daughters¦339826 will¦339827 be restored to¦339828 their¦339828 former¦339828 condition, and¦339829 Shomron¦339829 and her daughters will be restored \add ≈similarly\add*. Then¦339824 you¦339833 and¦339834 your daughters will¦339835 be restored to¦339836 your¦339836 former¦339836 condition.
\v 56 \add ≈You never even mentioned¦339842 your¦339841 sister¦339841 Sodom¦339840 in¦339843 the period when you were proud¦339845\add*,
\v 57 before¦339847 your¦339849 wickedness¦339849 was¦339848 revealed. But¦339856 now you're an object of scorn to the daughters of Aram¦339855 \add !(Syria¦339855)\add* and¦339856 to all¦339856 the¦339859 daughters¦339859 of¦339859 the¦339860 Philistines¦339860 around her¦339858. People all around despise¦339861 you¦339862.
\v 58 You'll display your¦339867 shame and¦339868 your¦339870 disgusting actions. That's Yahweh's¦339874 declaration¦339873.
\s1 The permanent agreement
\rem /s1 An Everlasting Covenant; A Covenant That Lasts Forever
\p
\v 59 The¦339881 master¦339880 Yahweh¦339880 says¦339879 this: ‘I'll¦339882 deal¦339882 with¦339884 you¦339884 as¦339885 you deserve—you who've despised¦339889 your oath¦339890 by¦339891 breaking¦339891 \add &our¦339892\add* agreement¦339892.
\v 60 But¦339894 I¦339895 myself will¦339894 call to¦339903 mind my¦339898 agreement with you that was made \add ≈when you were younger\add*, and¦339894 I'll¦339894 establish¦339902 a never-ending agreement with you.
\v 61 Then¦339907 you'll¦339907 call to mind your behaviour¦339910 and¦339911 be¦339911 ashamed¦339911 when¦339912 you¦339912 \add ≈adopt\add* your¦339915 older¦339916 and younger¦339920 sisters¦339915. I'll¦339922 give¦339922 them¦339923 to you as daughters¦339925, but¦339907 not¦339926 because of¦339927 your agreement¦339927.
\v 62 I myself will¦339929 establish¦339929 my¦339933 agreement¦339933 with¦339934 you¦339934, and¦339935 you'll¦339935 know¦339935 that¦339936 I am¦339939 Yahweh¦339939,
\v 63 so¦339941 that¦339941 you'll call everything to mind and¦339943 be¦339943 ashamed¦339943. Then you'll no longer open¦339949 your mouth¦339950 to speak¦339950, because of¦339960 your shame¦339952, when¦339953 I've forgiven¦339953 you for¦339955 everything¦339956 you've¦339959 done¦339959. That's¦339958 the¦339960 master¦339961 Yahweh's¦339962 declaration¦339960.’ ”
\c 17
\s1 Two eagles and the vine
\rem /s1 A Story of Two Eagles; The Two Eagles and the Vine; Two Eagles and a Vine; The Parable of the Eagles and the Vine
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦339968 \add ≈gave\add* me¦339969 \add another\add* message¦339966:
\v 2 “Son¦339982 of¦339972 humanity¦339974, present a riddle¦339975 and¦339977 tell¦339977 a parable¦339978 to the¦339981 \add ≈Israeli¦339981 people¦339974\add*.
\v 3 Tell¦339984 \add >them¦339984\add*, ‘The¦339991 master¦339989 Yahweh¦339989 says¦339987 this: ‘A large eagle¦339991, with large wings¦339994 full¦339997 of multi-coloured¦340002 feathers¦339996, and long¦339995 pinions, went¦340003 to¦340004 Lebanon¦340006 and¦340007 grabbed¦340007 hold of¦340010 the¦340011 top of a cedar¦340011 tree.
\v 4 He broke off¦340016 the top¦340014 shoot¦340015 of¦340015 \add @the tree\add* and¦340017 took¦340017 it¦340017 to¦340018 Canaan \add where he\add* placed¦340024 it in¦340022 a city¦340022 \add full\add* of merchants¦340021.
\v 5 He¦340026 \add ≈also¦340029\add* took¦340026 some of¦340027 the¦340027 land's¦340028 seed¦340032 and¦340026 planted it¦340026 in¦340030 fertile soil, \add ≈beside a large body of¦340030 water¦340036 where\add* a willow¦340038 \add might grow\add*.
\v 6 Then¦340041 \add @the¦340052 seed¦340052\add* sprouted¦340041 and¦340042 became a spreading vine¦340043 low¦340045 to¦340047 the ground. Its¦340048 branches turned¦340047 toward him¦340049, and¦340050 its¦340050 roots¦340050 grew \add ≈down below\add*, so it¦340051 became¦340053 a vine¦340054 and¦340055 produced¦340055 branches and¦340057 sent¦340057 out¦340057 shoots¦340056.
\p
\v 7 \add ≈But¦340060\add* there was¦340060 another large eagle¦340061 with large wings¦340066 and¦340067 many feathers¦340069. Oh¦340070 wow, that¦340072 vine¦340071 turned¦340073 its roots¦340074 toward this¦340072 eagle, and¦340076 it¦340077 spread out¦340077 its branches¦340076 toward the eagle from¦340082 the place it had been¦340060 planted¦340083 so it might get watered¦340080.
\v 8 It¦340093 had been¦340094 planted¦340094 in good¦340088 soil beside a large body of¦340100 water¦340091 so it¦340093 would grow branches¦340096 and¦340097 produce¦340098 fruit¦340098, to¦340085 become a magnificent vine¦340100.’
\p
\v 9 \add ≈Ask\add* \add the people\add*: ‘The¦340123 master¦340107 Yahweh¦340107 wants to know if it'll¦340120 prosper¦340109. Won't it¦340114 be uprooted and¦340115 stripped¦340119 of its fruit¦340117 so¦340105 that it withers¦340120, and all¦340121 its fresh¦340123 growth¦340124 will¦340125 dry out? \add ≈You wouldn't have to be very strong or get lots of people¦340130 to help\add* to pull¦340114 it out by¦340128 its roots¦340135.
\v 10 So¦340137 listen. After it¦340138 had been¦340138 planted¦340138, would¦340139 it¦340139 thrive¦340139? Wouldn't it¦340142 wither up when the eastern¦340144 wind¦340143 touches¦340141 it? \add Yes,\add* it would wither right up in¦340142 the garden plot where¦340150 it¦340151 sprouted.’ ”
\s1 The vine part of the parable explained
\rem /s1 The Riddle Explained; The Parable Is Explained
\p
\v 11 Then Yahweh¦340157 \add ≈gave\add* me¦340158 \add another\add* message¦340155:
\v 12 “\add ≈Ask\add* those rebellious¦340165 \add ≈people\add*, ‘Don't¦340166 you know¦340167 what¦340168 those things mean? Listen, the¦340175 king¦340175 of¦340175 Babylon came¦340174 to Yerushalem¦340178 and¦340179 captured¦340179 its king and its princes¦340185 and took¦340179 them¦340187 with him¦340188 to¦340189 Babylon.\x + \xo 17:12-15: \xt 2Ki 24:15-20; 2Ch 36:10.\x*
\v 13 Then he¦340191 took¦340191 \add a member\add* of¦340202 the royal¦340193 family¦340192, made¦340194 an¦340199 agreement¦340196 with¦340199 him—\add ≈forcing him to make¦340194 various commitments\add*. Then he took away the \add ≈country's\add* \add former\add* powerful people,
\v 14 so the kingdom¦340207 would remain \add ≈subjected and not¦340209 be¦340206 able to¦340209 become powerful again\add*. \add However,\add* by keeping the agreement¦340214, the \add ≈country\add* would \add at least\add* survive.
\v 15 But¦340217 the king of¦340221 Yerushalem rebelled¦340217 against him¦340219 by¦340220 sending¦340220 his¦340221 ambassadors¦340221 to Egypt¦340222 \add (Heb. Mitsrayim)\add* to acquire horses¦340226 and¦340217 an army. Will¦340230 he¦340230 succeed¦340230? Will¦340231 the¦340232 one¦340232 doing¦340232 these¦340233 things escape¦340231? If he¦340234 breaks¦340234 the agreement¦340235, will¦340236 he¦340236 \add ≈survive\add*?
\v 16 This is the master¦340242 Yahweh's¦340243 declaration¦340241: As I live¦340238, he'll¦340265 definitely die in the land of the king who¦340249 made¦340249 him¦340250 king, the king whose promises¦340255 he despised¦340252, and¦340256 whose agreement¦340260 he broke¦340257. He'll¦340265 die in the middle¦340262 of¦340262 Babylon¦340264.
\v 17 \add Egypt's\add* Far-oh¦340274 \add !(Pharaoh¦340274)\add* with¦340268 his mighty army¦340268 and huge¦340269 horde¦340270 won't¦340267 help him¦340273 in¦340268 battle¦340275, when¦340276 ramps are constructed and¦340278 siege¦340279 walls are built¦340278 up to¦340280 cut¦340280 off¦340280 many¦340282 lives¦340281,
\v 18 because the king despised¦340284 his¦340290 promise by¦340286 breaking¦340286 the¦340287 agreement¦340287. Wow¦340288, he reached out to make a promise, and¦340284 yet \add afterwards\add* he did¦340294 all¦340291 those¦340293 things. He¦340294 won't¦340295 escape¦340296.
\v 19 Therefore the¦340305 master¦340303 Yahweh¦340303 says¦340302 this: ‘As I live¦340305, wasn't it¦340317 my promise¦340311 that¦340312 he¦340313 despised¦340313 and¦340314 my agreement¦340314 that¦340315 he¦340316 broke¦340316? \add ≈Therefore\add* I'll¦340317 \add ≈cause him¦340317 to be punished for¦340299 what he¦340302 did\add*.
\v 20 I'll spread¦340320 my net¦340322 out over him, and¦340323 he'll¦340323 be¦340323 caught¦340323 in¦340324 my¦340324 trap, and¦340325 I'll take¦340325 him¦340325 to¦340326 Babylon¦340326 and¦340327 handle his¦340330 judgement¦340327 there¦340329 for the treason he committed when he betrayed me¦340334.
\v 21 All¦340337 of¦340337 his¦340339 refugees in¦340341 his¦340343 armies will be killed by¦340344 the sword¦340344, and¦340336 the ones who¦340346 remain will¦340350 be¦340350 scattered¦340350 in every¦340347 direction. Then¦340336 you \add people\add* will know¦340351 that¦340352 I¦340353 am Yahweh¦340354, because¦340352 I've¦340355 declared that that will happen.”
\s1 The tree-tip part of the parable explained
\rem /s1 God's Promise of Hope; Israel Exalted at Last
\p
\v 22 The¦340364 master¦340360 Yahweh¦340360 says¦340359 this, ‘So I myself will¦340362 take¦340362 away the highest part of¦340364 the¦340365 cedar¦340365 tree, and¦340367 I'll plant it away from¦340368 its¦340369 tender¦340370 branches. I'll break it off¦340371, and¦340372 I myself will¦340372 plant¦340372 it on¦340374 a¦340375 very high¦340377 mountain¦340375.
\v 23 I'll¦340383 plant¦340383 it on¦340398 Yisrael's¦340382 highest mountain¦340380 so it'll grow branches and¦340384 produce¦340384 fruit¦340387, and¦340388 it'll become a¦340389 majestic¦340390 cedar¦340389 so that every¦340393 winged bird¦340394 will¦340391 live under¦340392 it¦340392. They'll nest in¦340398 the¦340398 shade¦340398 of¦340398 its¦340399 branches¦340399,
\v 24 then¦340402 all¦340403 the¦340405 trees¦340405 in the¦340406 countryside¦340406 will know¦340402 that¦340407 I am Yahweh. I bring¦340410 down the high trees and I raise¦340414 up¦340414 the low¦340416 trees. I wither the watered tree¦340418 and¦340420 I cause the wilted tree¦340421 to bloom. I am Yahweh. I've¦340425 declared that that will happen, and¦340426 I will¦340426 do¦340426 it.’ ”
\c 18
\s1 Individual responsibility
\rem /s1 The Justice of a Righteous God; Individual Responsibility; The Soul Who Sins Will Die; Individual Retribution
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦340432 \add ≈gave\add* me¦340433 \add another\add* message¦340430:
\v 2 “What¦340436 do you mean, you \add people\add* who use this¦340444 proverb¦340440 about¦340447 Yisrael¦340448? You say¦340449, ‘Fathers eat¦340451 sour¦340452 grapes¦340452, \add ≈but¦340453 it's\add* the¦340443 children's¦340454 teeth¦340453 that¦340444 are¦340455 \add ≈set on¦340445 edge\add*’.
\p
\v 3 This¦340470 is the¦340457 master¦340461 Yahweh's¦340462 declaration¦340460: as I live¦340457, there'll \add ≈certainly no longer be any occasion for¦340466 you¦340466 to¦340468 use\add* this¦340470 proverb¦340468 in¦340471 Yisrael¦340471.
\v 4 Listen, every¦340474 life belongs to¦340477 me¦340477: the father's¦340480 life as well as the son's—they belong to¦340483 me¦340483. The¦340486 \add ≈one who disobeys\add* is the one who'll die¦340489.
\s2 The godly man
\p
\v 5 If¦340493 there's a \add ≈godly¦340496\add* \add >man¦340496\add* who does¦340497 what's fair and¦340492 right¦340496,
\v 6 who doesn't eat¦340505 at the¦340503 \add ≈hilltop\add* \add shrines\add*, who doesn't \add ≈request help\add* from Yisrael's¦340513 idols¦340511, who doesn't \add ≈mess with\add* someone else's wife¦340516 or a¦340522 menstruating¦340523 woman¦340522,
\v 7 who doesn't oppress¦340529 anyone¦340527, who gives back to debtors what they put up as security for loans, who doesn't \add ≈steal\add* \add but rather\add* gives his¦340530 food¦340536 to¦340537 the¦340537 hungry¦340537 and¦340539 \add ≈gives clothes¦340542 to those without them\add*,
\v 8 who doesn't charge too much interest¦340544 if he¦340547 lends¦340547 \add >money¦340547\add*, and¦340548 doesn't take¦340550 too much profit for¦340544 what he sells, who promotes true justice¦340554 \add ≈within the community\add*,
\v 9 who \add ≈follows\add* my instructions¦340561 and¦340563 \add ≈faithfully¦340566 obeys\add* my regulations¦340561, that man will be¦340567 \add ≈acquitted\add* \add and\add* will¦340570 definitely live¦340570. That's the¦340571 master¦340572 Yahweh's¦340573 declaration¦340571.\x + \xo 18:9: \xt Lev 18:5.\x*
\s3 The wayward son of the godly man
\p
\v 10 \add ≈But¦340575\add* suppose \add @that¦340579 godly man¦340583\add* has a violent¦340578 son¦340576 who¦340579 kills and¦340581 sadly \add ≈goes against all those¦340584 things above\add*,
\v 11 not¦340592 \add ≈following\add* the example of¦340602 his¦340603 \add ≈godly\add* father, but¦340586 \add rather\add* who's eaten¦340599 at the \add ≈hilltop\add* \add shrines\add* and¦340600 \add ≈slept with someone else's\add* wife¦340602,
\v 12 who oppresses¦340608 the¦340606 poor¦340606 and¦340607 needy¦340607, who steals and robs¦340610, who doesn't return¦340613 \add something given as\add* a pledge¦340611, who \add ≈requests help from\add* idols¦340616 and does¦340620 \add ≈disgusting things\add*,
\v 13 who lends¦340623 out money at too high interest¦340622, and¦340624 who makes too much profit on what he¦340625 sells. Should that man live¦340626? He certainly¦340635 won't¦340627! He'll¦340628 definitely die¦340635, and his blood¦340637 will¦340639 be¦340639 on \add ≈his own head\add*.
\s3 The peace/prosperity of child righteous/honest/sensible
\p
\v 14 But¦340641 listen, suppose he¦340642 has¦340642 a¦340643 son, and¦340644 his son sees¦340644 all¦340647 the¦340649 sins¦340649 that¦340651 his father's¦340650 committed, and¦340653 though he¦340653 sees¦340653 them¦340656, he doesn't do those¦340656 things.
\v 15 He¦340662 hasn't eaten¦340662 at the \add ≈hilltop\add* \add shrines\add*, and hasn't \add ≈requested help from the Israeli¦340670 people's idols¦340668\add*, and hasn't \add ≈slept with someone else's\add* wife¦340673,
\v 16 he¦340680 doesn't oppress¦340680 anyone¦340678, or \add ≈keep things given¦340689 as¦340683\add* a pledge¦340683, or \add ≈accept\add* stolen things, but¦340678 instead gives his¦340687 food¦340687 to¦340688 the¦340688 hungry¦340688 and¦340678 \add ≈gives clothes¦340693 to those without them\add*,
\v 17 he's¦340696 turned¦340696 his back¦340696 on¦340704 \add ≈crime\add*, and doesn't charge high interest¦340698, he¦340701 \add ≈follows\add* my¦340702 instructions¦340704 and \add ≈obeys\add* my regulations¦340704—he won't¦340700 die¦340708 for¦340709 his¦340710 father's¦340710 \add ≈evil¦340709 actions\add*, but¦340699 he'll¦340708 certainly¦340711 live¦340711.
\v 18 His¦340729 father¦340714, since¦340715 he¦340717 oppressed others by extortion¦340717 and robbed¦340719 \add ≈people\add*, and¦340722 did¦340726 \add ≈evil¦340732 things\add* among his people—listen, he'll¦340731 die¦340731 in¦340732 his¦340732 sin.
\p
\v 19 \add ≈But¦340734 you people ask¦340734\add*, ‘Why¦340735 doesn't the son \add also\add* have to \add pay the cost for his family's crimes\add*?’ \add Well\add* it's because the son \add ≈promotes\add* justice¦340743 and godliness and \add ≈follows\add* all¦340747 my¦340749 instructions¦340749. He'll¦340754 definitely live¦340753.
\v 20 The¦340756 one who sins¦340757 is the one who'll die¦340759. The children won't \add have to\add* \add ≈be responsible for\add* their parents¦340766' sin, and¦340767 the parents won't \add ≈be responsible for\add* their children's¦340771 sins—the¦340772 righteousness¦340772 of¦340772 those who act rightly¦340773 will¦340775 be¦340775 on themselves, and¦340776 the¦340776 wickedness¦340776 of the wicked¦340776 will¦340780 be¦340780 on themselves.\x + \xo 18:20: \xt Deu 24:16.\x*
\s2 Turning away from disobedience
\p
\v 21 \add ≈But¦340783\add* if¦340784 the¦340783 wicked¦340783 \add >person¦340783\add* turns¦340785 away¦340785 from¦340786 all¦340786 \add ≈their disobedience\add*, and¦340792 \add ≈follows\add* all¦340795 my¦340797 instructions¦340797 and¦340798 \add ≈does¦340798 what's right¦340800 and fair\add*, then \add @that¦340790 person¦340790\add* will¦340802 certainly¦340801 live¦340802 and not¦340803 die¦340804.
\v 22 All¦340806 \add ≈their acts of¦340806 disobedience\add* won't¦340811 be¦340812 called to¦340813 mind against them. They'll live¦340818 by the \add ≈right¦340814 things they¦340812 do¦340817\add*.
\v 23 That's the¦340822 master¦340825 Yahweh's¦340826 declaration¦340824.
\p Do¦340821 I¦340821 \add ≈celebrate happily\add* about the death¦340822 of¦340822 wicked¦340823 \add people\add*, and¦340830 not¦340827 about them turning¦340828 away from¦340829 their \add evil\add* behaviour¦340829 so that they can live¦340830?
\v 24 \add ≈But¦340833\add* if a righteous¦340834 person turns¦340833 away¦340833 from¦340835 their righteousness¦340835, and \add ≈disobeys\add* and \add ≈does¦340836 disgusting¦340836 things like¦340836\add* the wicked¦340843 people do¦340844, then will¦340845 they live¦340845? All¦340846 the \add ≈good things\add* that¦340850 had been¦340854 done¦340858 won't¦340853 be¦340854 called to¦340838 mind when¦340833 they¦340854 betray me in their treason, so they'll¦340854 die¦340864 in the sins¦340859 that they committed¦340836.
\p
\v 25 \add ≈But¦340866 you people complain\add* that the¦340869 master's¦340870 way¦340869 isn't¦340867 correct. Please¦340875 listen¦340871, \add you\add* \add ≈Israeli¦340874 people\add*: is it my¦340870 ways that aren't¦340867 correct, or is¦340878 it¦340878 \em your\em* ways¦340880?
\v 26 When¦340884 the¦340886 righteous¦340886 person turns¦340884 away¦340884 from¦340887 their righteousness¦340887, and¦340888 commits injustice¦340889 and¦340890 dies because¦340892 of¦340892 it, then \add *that person\add* will¦340896 die¦340890 in¦340892 the injustice¦340892 that¦340893 they've done¦340895.
\v 27 \add ≈But¦340899\add* when¦340899 a wicked person turns¦340899 away¦340899 from¦340901 the¦340900 wicked¦340900 things they've done¦340903 and \add ≈does¦340903 what's fair and what's right¦340906\add*, then \add *that¦340902 person¦340902\add* will¦340911 preserve¦340911 their life¦340910—
\v 28 they've \add ≈become aware of¦340918 all¦340916 their disobedient behaviours\add* and¦340913 turned¦340914 away¦340914 from¦340916 them. \add @That¦340919 person¦340919\add* certainly¦340921 won't¦340923 die¦340924, \add ≈but¦340913\add* will¦340922 live¦340922.
\v 29 \add ≈But¦340926 the¦340927 Israeli¦340928 people insist\add*, ‘The¦340931 master's¦340932 way isn't¦340929 fair!’ How is¦340930 my¦340932 way not¦340934 fair, \add ≈you Israeli¦340928 people\add*? It's¦340942 \em your\em* ways¦340933 that aren't¦340929 fair.
\v 30 Therefore I'll¦340947 judge¦340947 each¦340956 person among you according¦340946 to¦340946 their ways¦340946, \add ≈you Israeli¦340949 people\add*. That's the¦340951 master¦340952 Yahweh's¦340953 declaration¦340951.
\p \add ≈Change your direction¦340946\add* and¦340955 turn¦340955 away¦340955 from¦340956 all¦340956 your \add ≈disobedient behaviours\add* so¦340944 that they won't¦340959 be stumbling¦340963 blocks¦340963 of¦340958 evil¦340964 for¦340962 you.
