\v 3 “Son¦341212 of¦341212 humanity¦341214, tell¦341220 the Israeli¦341218 elders¦341218 that the master¦341238 Yahweh¦341239 says¦341223 this: ‘Have you \add people\add* come¦341229 to \add ≈get advice from me¦341227\add*? As I live¦341230, I won't \add ≈allow¦341235 you to ask¦341220 for¦341236 my¦341232 advice\add*. That's the master Yahweh's¦341225 declaration¦341237.’
\p
\v 4 Will¦341241 you¦341241 judge¦341241 them¦341242? Will¦341243 you¦341243 judge¦341243, son¦341244 of¦341244 humanity¦341246? Let them know¦341251 about¦341244 their¦341250 ancestors¦341250' \add ≈disgusting behaviour\add*.
\v 5 Tell them¦341254 that the master¦341258 Yahweh says¦341257 this: ‘On¦341260 the day¦341260 that I chose¦341261 Yisrael¦341262 and¦341253 made¦341268 myself¦341268 known¦341268 to them in¦341262 Egypt¦341271, I raised my¦341273 hand¦341273 to \add ≈make¦341268 a promise\add* to Yakov's¦341267 descendants¦341265. I told \add >them\add*, “I am¦341277 Yahweh your god¦341278”\x + \xo 20:5-6: \xt Exo 6:2-8.\x*—
\v 6 on that day¦341280 I raised¦341282 my¦341283 hand¦341283 to \add ≈make a promise\add* to them that I would bring¦341285 them¦341285 out¦341285 of¦341286 Egypt¦341287 into¦341288 a land¦341290 that¦341291 I'd carefully selected¦341293 for¦341294 them¦341294. It¦341299 was flowing¦341295 with milk¦341296 and¦341297 honey¦341297—it¦341299 was the most beautiful¦341298 of all¦341300 the¦341302 lands¦341302.
\v 7 I told¦341304 them¦341305, “Let each \add ≈family\add* throw¦341309 away¦341309 their Egyptian¦341311 idols¦341310, plus¦341310 \add ≈any other detestable¦341307 things¦341307 they have\add*. Don't¦341312 \add ≈defile¦341314\add* yourselves¦341314. I am¦341316 Yahweh¦341316 your¦341317 god¦341317.”
\v 8 \add ≈But¦341319\add* they¦341319 rebelled¦341319 against¦341321 me and¦341319 were¦341323 unwilling to¦341324 listen¦341324 to¦341325 me¦341325. \add *They¦341332\add* didn't¦341322 throw¦341332 away¦341332 the¦341335 detestable¦341329 things¦341329 \add ≈they¦341338 had\add* or abandon¦341338 their¦341330 Egyptian¦341348 idols¦341335, so I¦341339 determined to¦341340 pour¦341340 my fury¦341341 out¦341340 on¦341321 them to satisfy my rage¦341341 among them \add ≈right there\add* in¦341321 Egypt¦341336.
\v 9 I \add ≈did¦341350 that¦341357 to protect my¦341352 reputation¦341352\add* so it wouldn't be¦341354 \add ≈tarnished\add* in¦341360 the eyes¦341355 of¦341355 the¦341356 nations¦341356 \add ≈where they¦341359 were¦341360 staying\add*. I made¦341362 myself¦341362 \add ≈clearly\add* known¦341362 to¦341363 them¦341363\f + \fr 20:9 \ft them: Probably referring to those countries, but some translations interpret it to refer to the ones being brought out.\f* by¦341365 bringing¦341365 them¦341365 out¦341365 of¦341366 Egypt¦341367.
\p
\v 10 \add ≈So¦341369\add* I¦341372 led them out¦341369 of¦341370 Egypt¦341371 and¦341369 took them into¦341373 the¦341375 wilderness¦341375.
\v 11 Then¦341377 I¦341385 gave¦341377 them¦341378 my¦341381 instructions¦341381 and¦341377 regulations¦341381—\add ≈anyone who follows\add* them¦341386 will¦341388 live¦341391.\x + \xo 20:11-13: \xt Lev 18:5.\x*
\v 12 I also¦341394 \add ≈established rest days\add* as a sign¦341401 between¦341402 myself and¦341403 them—for them to¦341404 know¦341404 that¦341405 I am¦341407 Yahweh¦341407 who¦341408 \add ≈declares them¦341408 different from others\add*.\x + \xo 20:12: \xt Exo 31:13-17.\x*
\v 13 \add ≈But¦341410 the¦341413 Israeli¦341413 people¦341428\add* rebelled¦341410 against¦341412 me¦341412 in¦341416 the wilderness¦341416. They \add ≈wouldn't follow my instructions¦341417\add*, and¦341410 they¦341424 rejected¦341424 my regulations¦341417, \add even though\add* anyone who obeys them¦341427 will¦341429 live¦341429. They¦341434 severely¦341438 disrespected my rest days, so I¦341436 said¦341436 I'd pour¦341437 my fury¦341438 out¦341437 on¦341412 them in¦341417 the¦341428 wilderness in¦341430 order¦341436 to¦341441 end¦341441 them¦341441.
\v 14 \add ≈But¦341443 I did¦341443 that¦341450 to¦341446 protect my¦341445 reputation¦341445\add* so it wouldn't be¦341447 \add ≈tarnished\add* in the¦341448 eyes¦341448 of¦341448 the¦341449 nations¦341449, in whose sight¦341452 I had¦341451 brought¦341451 them¦341451 out¦341451 \add of Egypt\add*.
\v 15 So¦341454 I¦341456 myself \add ≈took¦341462 action by making a promise\add* to them in¦341460 the wilderness¦341460 not¦341461 to¦341462 bring¦341462 them¦341463 into¦341464 the¦341466 land¦341466 that¦341467 I'd been¦341473 going to give¦341469 them—a land flowing¦341470 with¦341460 milk¦341471 and¦341454 honey¦341472, which¦341467 was¦341473 the most beautiful¦341473 out of¦341458 all¦341475 the¦341477 lands¦341477.\x + \xo 20:15: \xt Num 14:26-35.\x*
\v 16 I promised that because¦341479 they'd rejected¦341481 my instructions¦341484 and not¦341485 \add ≈followed my regulations¦341484\add*, and they disrespected my rest days, because \add ≈what they really wanted was¦341497\add* their¦341495 idols¦341495.
\v 17 \add ≈But¦341499\add* I pitied¦341499 them¦341501, so I didn't¦341502 \add ≈wipe¦341501 them out¦341501\add* in¦341508 the wilderness¦341508.
\p
\v 18 I told¦341510 their children¦341513 in¦341514 the¦341515 wilderness¦341514, “Don't¦341517 \add ≈follow your¦341516 parents' habits or behaviour\add*, and¦341510 don't¦341517 defile¦341529 yourselves¦341529 with¦341514 their¦341522 idols¦341526.
\v 19 I am¦341532 Yahweh¦341532 your¦341533 god¦341533—\add ≈follow my instructions¦341534, obey my regulations¦341534\add*,
\v 20 and¦341543 keep¦341546 my¦341545 rest days \add different from other days\add* so that they'll¦341547 be¦341547 a sign¦341548 between¦341549 me¦341549 and¦341550 you. \add That way\add* you'll all know¦341551 that¦341552 I¦341553 am¦341554 Yahweh¦341554 your¦341555 god¦341555.”
\p
\v 21 \add ≈However\add*, their sons¦341560 and¦341557 daughters rebelled¦341557 against¦341559 me¦341559. They didn't¦341562 \add ≈keep¦341570 my instructions¦341561 or follow my regulations¦341561\add*, \add even though\add* anyone who obeys them¦341572 will¦341574 live¦341577. They¦341582 disrespected my rest days, so I¦341583 determined to¦341584 pour¦341584 my fury¦341585 out¦341584 on¦341559 them to satisfy my¦341581 rage¦341585 against them in¦341559 the¦341560 wilderness¦341590.
\v 22 \add ≈But¦341592 I¦341596 didn't¦341599 proceed, for¦341597 the¦341597 sake¦341597 of my¦341598 reputation¦341598\add*, so it wouldn't be¦341600 mocked by the nations¦341602 \add ≈who saw me\add* bring¦341605 the Israelis out¦341605 \add of Egypt\add*.
\v 23 \add ≈So I took action\add* in¦341617 the wilderness¦341617, \add promising that instead\add* I would scatter¦341618 them¦341619 among¦341620 the nations¦341620 and¦341621 disperse¦341621 them¦341622 into other countries¦341623.\x + \xo 20:23: \xt Lev 26:33.\x*
\v 24 I decided to do¦341629 that since they hadn't obeyed my instructions¦341630, and since they'd rejected¦341631 my regulations¦341630 and¦341632 disrespected my¦341634 rest days—\add ≈they really wanted\add* their¦341640 ancestors' idols¦341637.
\p
\v 25 Then¦341642 I¦341644 even gave¦341645 them¦341646 instructions¦341647 that weren't good¦341649, and¦341650 regulations¦341647 that¦341651 they¦341652 couldn't live¦341652 by¦341653.
\v 26 I declared them to be¦341670 defiled¦341655 \add ≈because of¦341657 the gifts¦341657 they gave\add* (they sacrificed every¦341659 \add ≈woman's\add* firstborn¦341661 child in¦341657 the fire) so¦341663 that¦341663 I could¦341664 fill them with¦341657 horror so¦341665 they¦341667 would know¦341667 that I am¦341670 Yahweh¦341670.’
\rem /s1 Judgment and Restoration
\p
\v 27 Therefore, son¦341679 of¦341677 humanity¦341681, speak¦341674 to¦341675 the¦341677 \add ≈Israeli¦341677 people¦341681\add* and¦341682 tell¦341682 them¦341683 that¦341689 the master¦341686 Yahweh¦341686 says¦341685 this¦341689: ‘That was also¦341682 how your¦341692 ancestors¦341692 blasphemed¦341690 me¦341691 when¦341693 they¦341690 were unfaithful¦341695 to me.
\v 28 When¦341697 I¦341702 brought¦341697 them¦341697 into¦341698 the¦341700 land¦341700 that¦341701 I'd promised to¦341706 give¦341706 them, then¦341697 whenever they¦341709 saw¦341709 any high¦341713 hill¦341712 and¦341714 leafy¦341717 tree¦341716, they¦341718 offered¦341728 their sacrifices¦341723. They¦341724 provoked¦341727 me with their offerings, and also¦341709 burnt their fragrant incense there¦341730 and¦341733 poured¦341733 out¦341733 their¦341737 drink¦341737 offerings.
\v 29 Then¦341739 I \add ≈asked¦341739\add* them¦341740, “What's¦341741 this high¦341742 place¦341742 where¦341743 you present your offerings?” so the¦341742 place is¦341742 called¦341748 Bamah¦341750 \add (meaning ‘High place’)\add* to¦341740 this day¦341752.’
