\v 47 Tell the forest that this is the master Yahweh's declaration: See, I'll set a fire among you. It'll burn up every \add ≈tree among you, whether living or dead\add*. The fiery flame won't \add be able to\add* be put out—every \add ≈area\add* from the north to the south will be burnt.
\v 48 Then \add ≈everyone\add* will see that I am Yahweh, when I light the fire, and it can't be extinguished.’ ”
\p
\v 49 Then I said, “Oh no, my master Yahweh, now they're \add ≈wondering if I'm just someone who tells\add* \add cute\add* parables.”
