\v 23 \add ≈but¦344358 instead\add* your turbans¦344358 will¦344359 be¦344359 on¦344359 your heads¦344361, and¦344362 your sandals¦344362 on¦344363 your feet¦344363. You won't¦344364 mourn¦344367 or weep¦344367, because you'll melt away¦344368 \add ≈due to¦344372 your disobedience\add*, and everyone will groan¦344370 for \add ≈their relatives¦344374\add*.
\v 24 \add ≈So¦344376\add* Yehezkel¦344377 will be a sign¦344379 for¦344378 you, because¦344387 when¦344385 that time comes¦344385, you'll do¦344384 \add ≈exactly the same as he's¦344383 doing\add*. Then¦344376 you \add people\add* will know¦344386 that¦344387 I¦344388 am the master¦344389 Yahweh¦344389.’ ”
\p
\v 25 “But¦344393 you, son¦344394 of¦344394 humanity¦344396, on¦344398 the¦344404 day¦344398 that I capture¦344399 their temple, (which is their joy¦344404, their¦344405 pride, and what they see and desire¦344408), and when I take¦344399 away their sons¦344414 and¦344415 daughters¦344415,
