\v 4 They'll¦344824 destroy¦344816 Tsor's¦344818 walls¦344817 and¦344819 tear¦344819 down¦344819 its towers¦344820, then¦344816 I'll¦344821 sweep its dust¦344822 away¦344821 and¦344824 make¦344824 it¦344825 like a bare rock¦344827.
\v 5 It'll become a place¦344829 in¦344832 the¦344832 middle¦344832 of¦344829 the¦344833 sea¦344833 for \add people to\add* spread¦344829 their nets¦344830 \add out to dry them\add*, since¦344834 I've¦344836 declared¦344837 it, and¦344840 it'll¦344831 become¦344840 plunder¦344841 for¦344842 the nations¦344842. That's the master¦344838 Yahweh's¦344839 declaration¦344837.
\v 6 Its¦344844 \add ≈young women¦344844\add* who are in¦344847 the¦344846 countryside¦344846 will¦344848 be¦344848 slaughtered¦344848 by swords¦344847, and¦344849 then¦344844 they'll¦344848 know¦344849 that¦344845 I¦344852 am¦344853 Yahweh¦344853.’
