\v 11 The¦344919 hooves¦344919 of¦344919 his¦344920 horses¦344920 will¦344921 trample¦344921 all¦344924 of¦344924 your streets¦344926. He'll¦344921 slaughter¦344929 your people¦344927 with¦344928 the sword¦344928 and¦344930 your mighty stone pillars¦344930 will \add ≈be knocked\add* to¦344932 the ground¦344932.
\v 12 They'll tear¦344939 down¦344939 your walls¦344940 and destroy your nice homes¦344941—plundering¦344935 your riches¦344936 and looting your merchandise¦344938. Then¦344935 they'll¦344935 throw your \add building\add* stones¦344944, wood¦344945, and¦344946 rubble¦344946 into¦344947 the¦344947 \add ≈ocean\add*.
