\v 18 Damascus¦345358 was¦345359 a trader¦345359 of¦345360 all your products¦345361, of all your enormous wealth¦345365, and of the¦345366 wine¦345366 from Helbon¦345367 and¦345368 the wool¦345368 from Zahar¦345369.\f + \fr 27:18 \ft Possibly, Zahar (used only once in the Hebrew scriptures) could refer to the white colour of the wool.\f*
\v 19 Dan and¦345372 Yavan¦345372 from¦345373 Uzal¦345373 \add ≈provided you with¦345374\add* merchandise of¦345374 wrought¦345377 iron¦345376, cinnamon, and¦345379 \add fragrant\add* calamus¦345379 \add seeds\add* which became your¦345380 merchandise.
