\v 7 I'll bring¦345689 foreigners against you¦345690—terrifying \add ≈warriors\add* from other nations¦345693. They'll bring their¦345695 swords¦345695 against the¦345698 beauty¦345698 of¦345692 your¦345699 wisdom¦345699, and¦345700 they'll¦345694 defile¦345700 your splendour¦345701.
\v 8 They'll send you¦345704 down¦345704 to¦345703 the¦345706 pit¦345703, and¦345705 you'll¦345705 die \add violently\add* like those who die at¦345708 sea¦345709.
\v 9 Will¦345712 you¦345712 really say¦345712, “I'm a god¦345713” to¦345715 the¦345715 face¦345715 of¦345715 one¦345716 who's¦345716 \add about to\add* kill¦345716 you? You're a man¦345716 and¦345719 not¦345719 God¦345713, and¦345717 you'll be¦345718 \add ≈at¦345722 the¦345722 mercy\add* of¦345722 the one who¦345723 \add ≈runs you¦345723 through\add*.
