\p
\v 1 \add ≈At the¦346881 end of¦346881 June\add* in¦346874 the eleventh year¦346876 \add since King Yoyakin (Jehoiachin) had been taken captive\add*,\f + \fr 31:1 \ft 587 B.C.\f* Yahweh¦346883 \add ≈gave me¦346884\add* a message¦346881:
\v 2 “Son¦346887 of¦346887 humanity¦346889, \add ≈ask¦346890\add* the¦346894 Egyptian¦346896 king¦346894 Far-oh¦346893 \add !(Pharaoh¦346893)\add* and¦346897 his¦346899 multitudes¦346899 around him, ‘\add ≈Who¦346902 else is¦346903 as powerful as you¦346903 and your¦346904 people¦346899\add*?
\v 3 Listen, Assyria¦346907 was¦346908 \add like\add* a cedar¦346908 in¦346909 Lebanon¦346909 with¦346909 beautiful¦346910 branches¦346911, giving¦346913 shade¦346913 to the forest¦346912—extremely tall¦346914, and¦346912 the branches¦346917 formed its¦346919 treetop¦346919.
\v 4 \add ≈A deep¦346923 water¦346921 supply\add* made¦346922 it¦346922 grow¦346922 tall. Rivers¦346927 flowed all around¦346929 its¦346927 area, because their channels¦346933 stretched out¦346934 to¦346935 all¦346936 the¦346938 trees¦346938 in the¦346939 countryside¦346939.
\v 5 It¦346944 \add ≈grew taller¦346944\add* than¦346946 any of the¦346947 other trees¦346947 in the¦346948 countryside¦346948, and its branches¦346952 grew long¦346951 and \add ≈thick\add* because¦346954 of \add ≈having plenty of\add* water¦346954 in its shoots¦346956.
