\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦347878 \add ≈gave\add* me¦347879 \add another\add* message¦347876:
\v 2 “Son¦347882 of¦347882 humanity¦347888, tell¦347891 this to¦347892 your people: ‘When I¦347896 \add ≈send an army\add* against any \add ≈country\add*, then the¦347900 people of that \add ≈country choose¦347899 one¦347904 of¦347905 their¦347905 men¦347903 to¦347909 become\add* a watchman¦347909 for¦347908 them¦347908.
\v 3 He¦347911 looks¦347911 for \add ≈any attacker coming¦347915 onto\add* the¦347918 land¦347918, and¦347911 then¦347911 he¦347919 blows¦347919 his horn¦347920 to warn¦347921 the¦347924 people¦347924.
\v 4 If the people hear¦347926 the sound¦347930 of¦347930 the¦347931 horn¦347931 but¦347926 don't¦347932 \add ≈take¦347933 any notice\add*, and¦347934 if the¦347935 \add ≈attacker\add* comes¦347934 and kills them, then¦347926 each one's¦347927 blood¦347937 is¦347939 on¦347938 their own¦347938 head¦347938.
