\v 6 \add ≈However,\add* if the¦347955 watchman¦347955 sees¦347958 the¦347961 \add ≈attacker\add* coming¦347962, \add ≈but\add* doesn't blow¦347965 the horn¦347966, \add ≈that is, if\add* the¦347967 people¦347967 weren't warned¦347970, and¦347971 if the¦347972 \add ≈attacker approaches\add* and¦347973 takes¦347973 anyone's¦347975 life, then¦347955 that person¦347967 dies in¦347966 their own sin, \add ≈but\add* I'll¦347983 require¦347983 their blood¦347979 from¦347974 the watchman¦347982.’
\p
\v 7 Now, \add ≈talking to\add* you, son¦347987 of¦347987 humanity¦347989: I've¦347991 made you a watchman¦347990 for¦347992 the¦347992 \add ≈Israeli¦347993 people¦347989\add*. You'll hear¦347994 the words¦347996 from¦347995 my mouth¦347995 and¦347997 then warn¦347997 them¦347998 on my behalf.
\v 8 If I say¦348001 to¦348002 a wicked¦348003 person, ‘You¦348005 wicked person, you're certainly about to die¦348005,’ and¦348006 if you don't¦348006 announce it so as to¦348008 warn¦348008 that wicked¦348009 \add person\add* about their behaviour¦348010, then that wicked¦348012 \add person\add* will¦348014 die in¦348013 their sin, but¦348006 \add ≈it'll be you¦348007 that I hold responsible for their death\add*.
\v 9 \add ≈But¦348019\add* if¦348020 you warn¦348022 the¦348023 wicked¦348023 person about¦348024 their behaviour, so that they might turn¦348025 back¦348025 from¦348026 it¦348026, and¦348019 if that person doesn't turn back from their behaviour, then¦348019 they'll die¦348033 in¦348032 their sin, but¦348019 you yourself will¦348033 have¦348036 saved¦348036 your¦348035 own life¦348035.
\s1 Each person is responsible for their own actions
\rem /s1 Individual Responsibility; The Watchman's Message; God's Justice and Mercy
\p
\v 10 \add ≈So,\add* son¦348040 of¦348040 humanity¦348042, you¦348049 tell¦348049 the¦348046 \add ≈Israeli¦348046 people¦348042\add*, ‘You're saying¦348049 this, “Our¦348053 errors and¦348054 our¦348054 disobedience \add ≈have¦348049 come back on¦348055 us¦348055 and they're hurting\add* us. How¦348059 can we¦348060 go on living¦348060 \add like this\add*?” ’
\v 11 Tell them¦348063 that this is the master¦348070 Yahweh's¦348071 declaration¦348068: ‘As I live, I don't delight¦348074 in¦348075 the¦348075 death¦348075 of¦348068 wicked¦348076 people. If¦348077 they turn¦348080 away from their wicked behaviour, then they'll live¦348083! \add ≈So turn¦348084 back¦348084\add*, \add yes\add* turn¦348085 away from¦348086 your wicked behaviour. Why should you \add ≈Israeli¦348090 people\add* die¦348089?’
\p
\v 12 \add ≈So now\add*, son¦348095 of¦348095 humanity¦348097, you tell¦348098 your¦348103 people¦348103, ‘Righteous¦348104 people's righteousness¦348105 won't save¦348107 them if they sin. Wicked¦348111 people's wickedness¦348111 won't cause them to die if they turn¦348117 away from¦348118 their sin. \add ≈No,\add* the¦348105 righteous¦348119 person¦348103 won't be¦348121 able¦348121 to¦348122 live¦348122 because of his¦348118 righteousness if he¦348125 sins¦348125.
\v 13 If I say¦348127 that a righteous¦348136 person will surely live¦348130, and if they¦348144 trust in¦348145 their righteousness¦348136 and then commit injustice¦348145, I won't¦348143 call to¦348128 mind any of¦348145 \add ≈the good things they did¦348148\add*—that person will¦348150 die¦348150 for the wickedness they committed.
\v 14 \add ≈Again,\add* if I say¦348152 to¦348153 the wicked¦348153, “You¦348155 will¦348155 surely¦348154 die¦348155,” but¦348152 if they then¦348152 turn¦348156 away from¦348157 their sins¦348157 and¦348158 do¦348158 what's just and¦348160 right¦348160,
\v 15 \add ≈like\add* returning¦348163 loan guarantees that were wickedly¦348164 demanded, or \add ≈like\add* making restitution for what they've stolen, and then if they \add ≈obey the¦348167 instructions¦348167\add* that give life¦348168 and no longer \add ≈disobey\add*, then \add @those¦348164 formerly¦348164 wicked¦348164 people¦348164\add* will¦348174 surely live¦348168—they won't¦348170 die¦348176.
\v 16 None of¦348178 the sins¦348180 that¦348182 they've committed will¦348185 be¦348185 called to¦348186 mind against them. Those who've acted justly and¦348188 rightly¦348188, will certainly¦348190 live¦348191.
\p
\v 17 But¦348193 your¦348195 people¦348195 say¦348193, “The¦348194 master's¦348199 way¦348198 isn't¦348196 fair!” but¦348193 it's¦348197 your ways that aren't¦348196 fair.
\v 18 When¦348206 the righteous¦348208 \add >person¦348208\add* turns¦348206 away from¦348209 \add ≈doing¦348210 what's right¦348208\add* and¦348210 \add ≈becomes disobedient\add*, then they'll die¦348212 in¦348213 \add @their¦348213 sin¦348213\add*.
