\p
\v 30 So now son¦348422 of¦348422 humanity¦348424, your¦348426 people¦348426 are¦348427 out¦348450 beside¦348429 the¦348430 walls¦348430 and¦348431 the¦348431 gates of¦348431 their houses¦348432 talking¦348427 about¦348422 you¦348428, and they're all telling¦348427 each¦348439 other, ‘Let's go and¦348447 listen¦348447 to¦348443 the¦348449 prophet's message¦348449 that¦348450 comes¦348450 from¦348451 Yahweh¦348452.’
\v 31 So¦348454 my¦348461 people¦348458 will come¦348454 to¦348455 you¦348455, as¦348456 they often do¦348468, and will sit¦348459 in¦348472 front¦348460 of¦348456 you and listen¦348462 to your¦348460 words, but they¦348462 won't¦348467 obey them¦348466. The¦348456 right words¦348465 are \add ≈on¦348472 their lips¦348472\add*, but their hearts¦348477 are¦348478 going¦348478 after¦348475 unjust¦348476 profit.
\v 32 \add ≈Yes,\add* you're like¦348482 a lovely song¦348482 to them, a beautiful¦348484 sound¦348485 that's¦348486 played¦348487 well¦348486 on a stringed instrument, so they'll listen¦348488 to your¦348491 words¦348491, but¦348480 none of¦348491 them will¦348482 obey them¦348494.
\v 33 So¦348496 when¦348496 all that happens, watch out, \add because it will indeed\add* happen. Then¦348496 they'll¦348499 \add ≈realise\add* that¦348500 a prophet's¦348501 been¦348502 among¦348503 them¦348503.”
\c 34
\s1 The ‘shepherds’ of Yisrael (Israel)
