\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦348509 \add ≈gave\add* me¦348510 \add another\add* message¦348507:
\v 2 “Son¦348513 of¦348513 humanity¦348515, prophesy¦348516 against Yisrael's shepherds. Prophesy¦348521 and¦348522 tell¦348522 them¦348523 that the master¦348529 Yahweh¦348529 says¦348527 this to¦348523 the¦348532 shepherds¦348532: Yisrael's¦348534 shepherds who¦348535 are¦348536 shepherding¦348537 themselves¦348538 \add ≈won't¦348539 end well\add*. Shouldn't shepherds guard the¦348540 flock¦348540?
\v 3 You eat¦348547 the \add ≈best sheep¦348552 meat\add* and¦348548 dress¦348551 in \add ≈woollen¦348550 clothes¦348551\add*. You slaughter¦348553 the \add ≈fat¦348552 lambs\add*. You don't¦348555 shepherd¦348556 at all.
\v 4 You haven't \add ≈taken¦348584 care¦348584 of¦348584 those\add* with diseases, nor do you heal¦348568 those who are ill. You don't bandage¦348571 up¦348571 the¦348574 ones \add ≈with broken limbs\add*, and¦348577 you don't restore the¦348579 outcasts or \add ≈search¦348584 for¦348584 those who've¦348584 gone¦348584 missing¦348584\add*. Instead, you use strength¦348562 and violence to¦348569 rule¦348583 over them¦348584.
\v 5 Then¦348587 they were scattered without a shepherd¦348589, and¦348587 after they were scattered, they¦348590 became¦348590 food¦348591 for¦348591 all¦348592 the¦348594 \add ≈wild animals¦348594\add* in the¦348595 countryside¦348595.\x + \xo 34:5: \xt Num 27:17; 1Ki 22:17; Mat 9:36; Mrk 6:34.\x*
\v 6 My¦348599 flock¦348599 has¦348613 strayed across all¦348600 the¦348602 mountains¦348602 and¦348603 onto every¦348604 high¦348607 hill¦348606, and¦348608 it's dispersed over¦348608 the entire¦348600 surface¦348611 of¦348611 the¦348612 earth¦348612, yet no one¦348616 is¦348617 searching¦348616 for them.
\p
\v 7 Therefore¦348621, you shepherds¦348621, listen¦348622 to Yahweh's¦348626 message¦348625 \add to you\add*:
\v 8 This is¦348651 the master¦348633 Yahweh's¦348634 declaration¦348631: As I live¦348628, my¦348633 flock has¦348639 become¦348644 plunder and food¦348646 for¦348646 all¦348647 the¦348649 wild animals¦348649 in the¦348650 countryside¦348650, because¦348651 there¦348651 wasn't any shepherd and \add ≡because\add* none of my shepherds \add ≈tried to¦348647 find any of¦348649\add* my flock \add that had gotten lost\add*. \add ≈Instead it was¦348651 themselves¦348662 that\add* the shepherds looked after, and¦348663 they¦348667 didn't¦348637 shepherd¦348652 my flock.
\v 9 Therefore¦348671, \add you so-called\add* ‘shepherds¦348671’¦348671, listen¦348672 to Yahweh's¦348675 message¦348673:
\v 10 The¦348685 master¦348680 Yahweh¦348680 says¦348679 this: Listen, I'm¦348682 against¦348683 those shepherds¦348685. I'll require \add ≈compensation from¦348690 them¦348691 for\add* my flock¦348693, and¦348694 then I'll dismiss them from shepherding¦348692 the¦348698 flock. Those shepherds won't shepherd¦348696 themselves¦348699 any longer \add either\add*, \add ≈because\add* I'll take my flock away from¦348702 their¦348702 mouths¦348702, so that my flock won't become¦348705 food¦348707 for them any longer.
\s1 The evil shepherds
\rem /s1 God, the True Shepherd; The Good Shepherd
\p
\v 11 \add ≈So¦348711\add* the master¦348713 Yahweh¦348713 says¦348712 this: Listen, I myself will¦348718 search¦348718 for¦348718 \add those lost from\add* my¦348721 flock¦348721, and¦348722 I \add ≡myself\add* will look¦348718 after them¦348722,
\v 12 like¦348724 a shepherd¦348725 searches¦348724 for his¦348726 sheep¦348732 when he's¦348729 among¦348730 his¦348732 scattered flock¦348732. So¦348734 I'll look¦348735 for my¦348738 flock and¦348739 I'll rescue¦348739 them¦348740 from¦348741 all¦348741 the¦348743 places¦348743 where¦348744 they¦348745 were¦348745 scattered¦348745 \add ≈during¦348747 the dark¦348749 times\add*.
\v 13 I'll bring¦348751 \add @my¦348754 people¦348754\add* out¦348751 from¦348752 among the¦348754 \add ≈nations¦348754\add*. I'll gather¦348755 them¦348755 from¦348756 \add foreign\add* lands¦348758 and¦348759 bring¦348759 them¦348759 \add back\add* to¦348760 their¦348762 land. I'll put them¦348763 in¦348768 pastures on¦348768 Yisrael's¦348767 mountainsides¦348766, by the streams, and¦348769 in¦348769 every¦348769 settlement in the land¦348771.
\v 14 I'll¦348776 put them¦348777 in good pastures—Yisrael's high¦348779 mountains¦348778 will¦348785 be¦348782 their¦348783 grazing places. They'll lie¦348785 down¦348785 there¦348784 in¦348786 places good¦348787 for grazing, in abundant pastures, and¦348788 they'll¦348785 graze¦348790 on¦348778 Yisrael's hills¦348778.
\v 15 I myself will¦348797 shepherd¦348797 my¦348798 flock¦348798, and¦348799 I myself will¦348800 \add ≈give them¦348800 rest¦348800\add*. That's the¦348801 master¦348802 Yahweh's¦348803 declaration¦348801.
\p
\v 16 I'll search¦348808 out the lost¦348807 and restore the outcast. I'll bandage¦348814 up¦348814 those who are broken and¦348815 heal those who are sick¦348817, but¦348809 I'll destroy¦348825 those who are fat¦348821 and well. I¦348808 will¦348818 shepherd¦348826 with¦348827 justice¦348827.
\p
\v 17 So¦348829 now this is what the¦348842 master¦348833 Yahweh¦348833 says¦348832, You, my¦348833 flock¦348830, listen, I'll be a judge¦348836 between¦348837 one sheep¦348839 and¦348840 another, and¦348841 between rams¦348841 and¦348842 billy goats¦348842.
\v 18 Isn't it enough¦348844 to feed on¦348852 the good¦348847 pasture¦348846? Do you have to trample¦348851 down \add ≈any remaining¦348858 grass\add*? Or drink¦348856 from clear¦348853 waters¦348855, then muddy¦348860 the streams with¦348852 your feet¦348852?
\v 19 Must my¦348862 flock¦348862 eat what you've trampled¦348863 and¦348862 drink¦348868 what you've muddied with your¦348864 feet¦348864?
\p
\v 20 Therefore the master¦348874 Yahweh¦348874 says¦348873 this to¦348876 them¦348876: Listen, I¦348877 myself will¦348880 judge¦348880 between¦348881 the fat¦348884 sheep¦348886 and¦348885 the thin ones,
\v 21 because¦348889 you \add shepherds\add* have¦348900 pushed¦348892 them with your sides¦348890 and¦348891 shoulders¦348891, and¦348893 you've gored¦348894 all¦348895 the¦348897 weak¦348897 ones with your horns¦348893 until¦348898 you \add succeeded in\add* scattering¦348900 them¦348901 away from the¦348904 land.
\v 22 I'll save¦348906 my¦348907 flock¦348907 and¦348908 they'll¦348910 no longer be \add taken as\add* plunder, and¦348913 I'll judge¦348913 between¦348914 one sheep¦348915 and¦348916 \add ≈the next\add*.
\v 23 I'll¦348918 set one¦348921 shepherd over¦348919 them—my servant¦348925 David¦348926. He'll¦348922 \add ≈look after\add* them, and¦348918 he'll¦348922 be their shepherd.\x + \xo 34:23: \xt Rev 7:17.\x*
\v 24 Then¦348936 I, Yahweh, will¦348938 be their¦348944 god¦348940, and¦348941 my¦348941 servant¦348941 David¦348942 will¦348943 be a leader¦348943 among¦348944 them¦348944. I, Yahweh, have¦348947 declared that.\x + \xo 34:24: \xt Eze 37:24.\x*
\rem /s1 The Lord's Covenant of Peace
\p
\v 25 Then¦348949 I'll¦348953 make¦348949 a¦348951 peace¦348952 treaty¦348951 with¦348961 them¦348950 and¦348953 remove the wild¦348956 animals¦348954 from¦348957 the¦348959 land¦348959, so that they'll¦348960 \add be able to\add* live¦348960 securely¦348962 in the wilderness¦348961 and¦348963 sleep¦348963 safely in¦348964 the forests¦348964.
\p
\v 26 I'll¦348966 also¦348968 \add ≈bless¦348970\add* \add both\add* them¦348967 and¦348968 the places around¦348968 my¦348969 hill¦348969, and¦348971 send¦348971 out showers in¦348973 the right season¦348973—they'll¦348976 be¦348976 showers of¦348968 blessing¦348975.
\v 27 Then¦348978 the¦348979 trees¦348979 in the¦348980 countryside¦348980 will produce their fruit¦348983, the¦348984 soil will¦348985 yield its¦348986 produce, and¦348987 my sheep will¦348987 be¦348987 secure¦348991 in their land¦348990. When¦348978 I break¦348997 \add ≈off the ties holding the yoke¦349001\add* \add onto their necks\add*, and when¦348997 I rescue¦349002 them¦349002 from¦349003 the¦349003 \add ≈control\add* of¦349003 those¦349004 who¦349004 enslaved¦349004 them, then¦348978 they'll¦348987 know¦348992 that¦348993 I am¦348996 Yahweh¦348996.
\v 28 They'll no longer be¦349009 plunder¦349011 for¦349012 the \add other\add* nations¦349012, and¦349013 the¦349013 wild animals¦349013 on the¦349014 land¦349014 will¦349016 no longer devour¦349016 them. Then¦349007 they'll¦349009 live¦349017 securely¦349018, and¦349019 no one¦349020 will \add ≈make them afraid\add*.
\v 29 I'll¦349022 provide¦349022 a land¦349032 for them¦349023 that's known for¦349025 its crops, so they won't be victims of¦349030 famine¦349031, and¦349022 they won't be \add ≈mocked by\add* \add other\add* nations¦349038.
\v 30 Then¦349040 they'll¦349040 know¦349040 that¦349041 I¦349042, Yahweh¦349052 their¦349044 god¦349044, am¦349047 with¦349045 them¦349045. The¦349050 \add ≈Israeli¦349048 people\add* are¦349047 my¦349047 people. That's¦349041 the¦349048 master¦349051 Yahweh's¦349043 declaration¦349050.
\p
\v 31 You are¦349055 my sheep¦349055, the¦349056 flock¦349056 of¦349056 my¦349057 pasture¦349057, and my¦349057 people, and I¦349060 am¦349061 your¦349061 god¦349061. That's the¦349062 master¦349063 Yahweh's¦349064 declaration¦349062.’ ”
\c 35
\s1 Edom's coming punishment
