\v 10 You've said¦349201, “These two¦349204 nations¦349205 and¦349206 these two¦349208 lands¦349209 will¦349211 become mine, and¦349212 we'll¦349212 possess¦349212 them,” even when Yahweh¦349213 was¦349215 there¦349214 with them.
\v 11 Therefore, this is the¦349218 master¦349222 Yahweh's¦349223 declaration¦349221: As¦349233 I live¦349218, I'll act¦349224 according¦349225 to¦349225 your¦349225 anger¦349225 and¦349226 according¦349226 to¦349226 your¦349226 jealousy¦349226 that¦349227 you¦349228 had in¦349230 your hatred¦349229 of¦349220 Yisrael, and I'll show myself¦349231 to them¦349232 when I judge¦349234 you¦349234—
\v 12 then¦349236 you'll¦349236 know¦349236 that¦349248 I¦349239 am¦349240 Yahweh¦349240. I've¦349241 heard¦349241 all¦349245 the¦349252 insults you spoke¦349249 against Yisrael's¦349253 \add ≈hill¦349252 country\add*, when you said¦349249, “They've been¦349256 destroyed—they've¦349256 been¦349259 given¦349259 over to us¦349258 to devour.”
\v 13 You¦349262 raised yourselves¦349262 up against me¦349263 with¦349264 what you said, and¦349265 you multiplied¦349265 the words¦349267 you said against me, and I¦349268 heard¦349269 all of¦349267 them.
\p
\v 14 The¦349275 master¦349274 Yahweh¦349274 says¦349273 this: I'll¦349281 make¦349281 you¦349283 \add ≈into a desolate¦349280 place\add* while the \add ≈rest of¦349277 the¦349279 world¦349279 cheers\add*.
\v 15 Just like you rejoiced¦349285 over the Israeli¦349287 people's inheritance¦349286 \add ≈when it¦349293 was¦349293 made desolate¦349293\add*, I'll¦349295 do¦349295 the same to¦349297 you¦349297. You'll become a desolation¦349298, Mt¦349300. Seir¦349302 and¦349303 all¦349303 of Edom¦349305—all of¦349306 it¦349306. Then they'll¦349307 know¦349307 that¦349308 I¦349310 am¦349311 Yahweh¦349311.”
\c 36
\s1 God's blessing for Yisrael (Israel)
\rem /s1 Blessing on Israel; A Prophecy to the Mountains of Israel; Restoration for Israel; God's Blessing on Israel
\p
\v 1 “Now, son¦349315 of¦349315 humanity¦349317, prophesy¦349318 to¦349319 Yisrael's¦349322 mountains¦349321 and¦349323 say¦349323, ‘Mountains¦349324 of¦349324 Yisrael¦349325, listen¦349326 to Yahweh's¦349329 message¦349327.
\v 2 The master¦349333 Yahweh¦349333 says¦349332 this: The¦349337 enemy¦349337 has¦349343 said¦349336, “Aha¦349339,” \add when talking\add* about¦349340 you¦349338, and¦349340 “The¦349340 ancient¦349341 \add ≈hilltop¦349340 shrines¦349340\add* have become¦349343 ours.” ’
\p
\v 3 Therefore¦349352 prophesy¦349347 and¦349348 tell¦349348 them that the master¦349351 Yahweh¦349351 says¦349350 this: Because¦349353 of your desolation¦349355 and because¦349353 of the attacks that came on¦349354 you from¦349358 all sides¦349358, you've \add ≈ended up¦349363 belonging to¦349359\add* other nations¦349362—you've been¦349363 the subject of slanderous¦349368 lips¦349366 and tongues¦349367, and¦349368 of¦349368 people's¦349370 stories.
\v 4 Therefore, mountains¦349373 of¦349373 Yisrael¦349374, listen¦349375 to the message¦349376 from¦349400 the master Yahweh: The¦349376 master Yahweh says¦349382 this to¦349385 the mountains¦349385 and¦349386 the high hills¦349386, to¦349387 the streambeds and¦349388 valleys¦349388, to¦349389 the \add ≈places¦349389 that have been¦349400 destroyed and are¦349400 now uninhabited\add*, and to the forsaken cities¦349391 that have become¦349394 plunder¦349395 and a subject of mocking for¦349372 the other nations¦349398 that¦349399 surround them—
\v 5 the master¦349407 Yahweh¦349407 says¦349406 this: I've¦349414 certainly spoken¦349414 in the \add ≈heat\add* of¦349412 my¦349413 anger against the other nations¦349418, against Edom¦349421 and everyone¦349433 who took my land for themselves as a possession¦349431—against all¦349422 those who had¦349414 both celebration in¦349431 their heart¦349435 and disdain in their spirit as they seized my land so¦349404 they¦349424 could claim its¦349439 pasturelands¦349439 for themselves.’
\p
\v 6 Therefore, prophesy¦349443 to¦349449 Yisrael¦349447 and¦349448 tell¦349448 the mountains¦349449 and¦349450 the high hills¦349450, the streambeds and¦349452 the valleys¦349452, that the master¦349457 Yahweh¦349457 says¦349455 this: Listen, in¦349460 my¦349460 fury¦349461 and in¦349461 my anger¦349461 I'm declaring this because¦349463 you've¦349466 endured¦349466 insults¦349464 from \add other\add* nations¦349465.
\v 7 Therefore, the master¦349471 Yahweh¦349471 says¦349470 this: I¦349473 myself will \add ≈take action and promise\add* that the¦349481 nations¦349481 that¦349482 surround you¦349483 will¦349488 certainly \add be made to\add* carry¦349488 their¦349486 own shame.
\v 8 But¦349490 you Israeli mountains¦349491, you'll grow branches¦349493 and¦349495 bear¦349496 fruit¦349495 for¦349497 my¦349497 Israeli people¦349497, since¦349499 they'll soon come¦349501 back to¦349501 you,
\v 9 because¦349503, listen, I'm¦349504 for¦349503 you, and¦349506 I'll¦349506 treat you favourably—you'll be¦349508 ploughed and¦349509 sown¦349509 \add with seed\add*.
\v 10 I'll¦349511 multiply¦349511 \add ≈your population—all¦349514 the¦349516 Israeli¦349517 people\add*. The¦349520 cities¦349520 will¦349522 be¦349522 inhabited¦349519 \add again\add* and¦349511 the¦349521 ruins¦349521 rebuilt¦349522.
\v 11 I'll increase¦349528 \add both\add* people and animals¦349527 on¦349525 you \add ≡mountains\add* so that they'll¦349528 multiply¦349524 and be¦349529 fruitful¦349529. Then¦349524 I'll cause¦349530 you to¦349530 be¦349530 inhabited¦349530 like¦349532 you were previously, and I'll make¦349530 you prosper more¦349534 than¦349534 you did¦349533 in the past \add ≈so that\add* you'll know¦349535 that I¦349530 am¦349539 Yahweh¦349539.
\v 12 I'll¦349541 bring my¦349546 Israeli people¦349546 to walk¦349541 on¦349542 you. They'll possess¦349548 you¦349548, and¦349549 you'll be their inheritance¦349551, and you'll no longer cause¦349541 their children to die.
\p
\v 13 The master¦349561 Yahweh¦349561 says¦349560 this: They're telling¦349564 you¦349568, “You¦349573 \add ≡mountains\add* devour¦349566 people¦349564, bereaving¦349570 your¦349571 nation¦349571 of¦349566 children,”
\v 14 therefore you won't¦349577 consume¦349579 people any longer, and¦349581 you'll¦349579 no longer make your¦349581 nation¦349581 mourn their deaths. That's the¦349588 master¦349589 Yahweh's¦349590 declaration¦349588.
\v 15 I¦349594 won't¦349592 allow you to hear¦349594 the¦349597 insults¦349597 from the¦349598 \add other\add* nations¦349598 any longer—you'll¦349602 no longer have to bear¦349602 the people¦349600 groups shaming you, and¦349592 you won't cause¦349609 your¦349605 nation¦349605 to¦349609 stumble¦349609. That's the¦349611 master¦349612 Yahweh's¦349613 declaration¦349611.”
\rem /s1 The Renewal of Israel; Israel's New Life
\p
\v 16 Then Yahweh¦349619 \add ≈gave\add* me¦349620 \add another\add* message¦349617:
\v 17 “Son¦349623 of¦349623 humanity¦349625, when the¦349626 \add ≈Israeli¦349626 people¦349625\add* inhabited¦349628 their land¦349631, they¦349632 defiled¦349632 it¦349633 with¦349634 their¦349634 customs and¦349635 their activities. \add ≈In¦349627 my¦349640 eyes,\add* their customs were¦349628 like¦349636 the¦349636 uncleanness¦349636 of¦349636 a woman's menstruation¦349637,
\v 18 \add ≈so\add* I poured¦349642 out¦349642 my¦349643 fury¦349643 against them¦349644 for the¦349647 blood¦349647 that¦349648 they'd poured¦349650 out¦349650 on¦349654 the land¦349653, and¦349642 for how they'd polluted it¦349655 with¦349654 their¦349654 idols¦349654.
\v 19 I scattered¦349657 them¦349658 among¦349659 the nations¦349659—they¦349660 were¦349660 dispersed¦349660 through the lands¦349661. I judged¦349664 them according¦349662 to¦349662 their customs and¦349657 their¦349662 actions¦349662.
\v 20 Then¦349666 they went¦349666 to¦349667 those¦349684 \add other\add* nations¦349669, and¦349666 wherever¦349670 they¦349672 went¦349672, they¦349674 profaned¦349674 my holy name¦349677 when¦349679 people asked¦349679 about¦349677 them¦349680, ‘Are¦349681 these¦349684 really Yahweh's¦349683 people? After all, they've¦349686 been¦349681 thrown out¦349686 of¦349677 his¦349685 land¦349685.’
\v 21 \add ≈But¦349688\add* I¦349696 had compassion for my holy name¦349691 that¦349693 the¦349695 \add ≈Israeli¦349695 people\add* had defiled¦349694 among¦349697 the \add other\add* nations¦349697, when they¦349700 went¦349700 there¦349701.
\p
\v 22 Therefore tell¦349705 the¦349706 \add ≈Israeli people\add* that¦349725 the master¦349711 Yahweh¦349711 says¦349710 this: I'm¦349715 not¦349713 doing this for¦349714 the sake¦349714 of¦349717 you \add ≈Israeli people\add*, but for my¦349711 sacred¦349724 name¦349722, which¦349725 you've profaned¦349726 among¦349727 the nations¦349727 everywhere you've gone¦349730.
\v 23 My¦349736 great¦349737 name¦349736, which¦349740 you \add people\add* have¦349741 profaned among the nations, I'll¦349733 make holy¦349733 \add even\add* among the nations \add where\add* you profaned it. Then¦349733 the nations will¦349733 know¦349743 that¦349740 I¦349747 am¦349748 Yahweh¦349751, when¦349752 they¦349743 see¦349743 you recognise¦349743 my¦349736 holiness¦349733. That's¦349745 the¦349749 master¦349750 Yahweh's¦349748 declaration¦349749.
\v 24 I'll take¦349756 you \add back\add* out of¦349770 those nations¦349760 and¦349761 gather¦349761 you from¦349763 every¦349763 land¦349765, and¦349766 I'll bring¦349766 you into¦349768 your land¦349770.
\v 25 Then¦349772 I'll sprinkle¦349772 pure¦349775 water¦349774 on¦349773 you so you'll be¦349776 cleaned¦349776 from¦349777 all¦349777 of¦349778 your impurities¦349778, and¦349772 I'll purify¦349782 you from all your idols¦349781.
\v 26 I'll give¦349785 you \add people\add* a new heart and a new spirit¦349789 in¦349792 your¦349792 innermost¦349792 parts¦349792, and¦349793 I'll take¦349793 the¦349796 stony heart¦349796 away from¦349798 your \add ≈bodies\add* and \add ≈replace it with¦349792\add* a heart¦349801 of¦349801 flesh¦349802.\x + \xo 36:26-28: \xt Eze 11:19-20.\x*
\v 27 I'll¦349807 put¦349807 my spirit¦349806 in¦349808 you and¦349809 enable you \add Israelis\add* to \add ≈follow my instructions¦349813 and¦349815 keep¦349816 my regulations¦349813\add*.
\v 28 Then¦349819 you'll inhabit¦349819 the¦349820 land¦349820 that¦349821 I¦349822 gave¦349822 to¦349823 your ancestors¦349823—you'll be¦349824 my people¦349826 and¦349819 I'll¦349828 be your god¦349830.
\v 29 I'll save¦349832 you from¦349834 all¦349834 of¦349835 your uncleanness¦349835, and then¦349832 I'll summon¦349836 the¦349839 grain¦349839 and¦349840 multiply¦349840 it¦349841—I'll no longer \add ≈assign\add* famine¦349846 to¦349845 you.
\v 30 I'll¦349848 multiply¦349848 the¦349851 \add #fruit¦349851 on¦349862 the trees¦349852\add* and¦349853 the¦349853 produce¦349853 \add ≈from the¦349854 soil\add* so¦349855 that¦349855 you'll no longer \add ≈be shamed by other nations¦349862 seeing you suffering\add* famine¦349861.
\v 31 Then¦349864 you'll think¦349864 about¦349867 your wicked¦349868 customs¦349867 and¦349869 your activities that¦349870 weren't good¦349873, and¦349874 \add ≈your faces¦349875 will¦349874 display your loathing¦349874 of¦349869 your own sins and¦349878 your disgusting habits\add*.
\v 32 But¦349892 make sure you know¦349889 this: I'm¦349883 not doing all that for¦349882 \em your\em* sake¦349882, \add ≈so you Israeli¦349894 people\add* should¦349889 be¦349889 ashamed¦349891 and¦349892 disgraced because of¦349893 your \add ≈behaviour¦349893\add*. That's¦349895 the¦349886 master¦349887 Yahweh's¦349888 declaration¦349886.
\p
\v 33 The¦349910 master¦349900 Yahweh¦349900 says¦349899 this: \add ≈When\add* I¦349903 purify¦349903 you from¦349905 all¦349905 your disobedience, I'll¦349907 enable you to¦349907 inhabit¦349907 the cities¦349910 \add again\add* and¦349911 to rebuild¦349911 the¦349912 ruined¦349912 places¦349912,
\v 34 and¦349914 the¦349914 idle land¦349914 will¦349916 be¦349916 tilled¦349916 until it's¦349919 no longer a¦349920 wasteland¦349920 for everyone¦349922 to¦349921 see as they go¦349924 past.
\v 35 Then¦349926 \add instead\add* they'll say¦349926, “This¦349928 land¦349927 was desolate¦349935, but¦349926 it's¦349930 become¦349930 like¦349931 the¦349931 garden¦349931 of¦349931 Eden¦349933—the¦349934 abandoned cities¦349934 and the¦349935 uninhabited ruins¦349935 that¦349928 were torn¦349937 down¦349937 are now fortified¦349938 and inhabited.”
\v 36 Then¦349941 the¦349942 other nations¦349942 around¦349945 you¦349945 will know¦349941 that¦349943 I am¦349944 Yahweh, because¦349946 I built¦349950 up the¦349951 ruins and replanted the¦349953 abandoned places¦349953. I, Yahweh, have¦349956 declared it and¦349957 I will¦349957 do¦349957 it.
\p
\v 37 The master¦349962 Yahweh¦349962 \add also\add* says¦349961 this¦349965: The¦349967 \add ≈Israeli¦349969 people\add* will¦349966 again¦349964 ask¦349961 me to do¦349970 this for¦349971 them¦349971: to increase¦349972 \add ≈their population like¦349974 sheep¦349974\add*.
\v 38 Just like the flock¦349987 \add ≈that's¦349990 kept separate to be used\add* for sacrifices (like the flock in¦349981 Yerushalem¦349980 at¦349981 its¦349981 scheduled feasts¦349981), so¦349982 too the ruined¦349985 cities¦349984 will be filled with¦349981 flocks¦349987 of¦349977 people and¦349989 they¦349983 will know¦349989 that I¦349992 am¦349993 Yahweh¦349993.”
\c 37
\s1 The valley with bleached bones
\rem /s1 A Valley of Dry Bones; The Valley of Dry Bones
\p
\v 1 \add ≈One¦350003 day Yahweh¦350000 gave me another vision\add*, and¦350001 he¦350001 took¦350001 me¦350001 out¦350001 by¦350002 his spirit¦350002 and¦350004 put¦350004 me¦350004 down¦350004 in¦350002 the¦350005 middle¦350005 of¦350006 a valley¦350006 that was¦350008 full¦350008 of bones¦350009.
\v 2 Then¦350011 he¦350011 led me¦350011 all¦350013 around¦350011 them¦350012, and wow, there were so many¦350013 bones¦350017 in the¦350021 valley¦350022, and¦350023 they¦350024 were¦350024 totally dried¦350024 out!
\v 3 “Son¦350029 of¦350029 humanity¦350031,” he¦350027 \add ≈asked\add* me¦350028, “can these¦350034 bones¦350033 become living¦350032 \add people\add* again?”
\p “My¦350036 master¦350036 Yahweh¦350036,” I¦350035 \add ≈replied¦350027\add*, “\add ≈only you¦350038 would¦350032 know¦350039 that\add*.”
\p
\v 4 Then¦350041 he¦350041 told¦350041 me¦350042, “Prophesy¦350043 over these¦350047 bones and¦350041 tell¦350041 them¦350049, ‘Dry¦350051 bones. Listen¦350050 to¦350042 Yahweh's¦350055 message¦350053.
\v 5 The¦350062 master¦350059 Yahweh¦350059 says¦350058 this to¦350061 these¦350062 bones¦350061: Listen, I'm¦350064 about¦350065 to¦350065 put breath¦350067 into you, and¦350068 you'll live¦350068.
\v 6 I'll \add ≈connect\add* sinews to¦350071 you and¦350073 put flesh¦350075 onto you. I'll cover¦350076 you with¦350080 skin¦350078 and¦350079 put¦350079 breath¦350081 into you so you'll live¦350082. Then¦350070 you'll know¦350083 that¦350084 I¦350073 am¦350087 Yahweh¦350087.’ ”
\p
\v 7 So¦350089 I prophesied¦350089 as¦350090 I was¦350091 instructed¦350091, and¦350089 wow, a sound¦350094 like¦350095 something rattling¦350098 started as the¦350100 bones¦350100 moved together¦350099—bone¦350101 against bone¦350104!
\v 8 I¦350107 looked¦350106 and, wow, the bones now had sinews on¦350119 them, and flesh¦350111 grew up¦350112 \add over that\add*, and then¦350106 skin¦350115 covered¦350113 them! \add ≈But¦350106\add* there¦350118 was¦350118 still no breath in¦350119 them¦350119.
\p
\v 9 Then¦350121 Yahweh told¦350121 me¦350122, “Prophesy¦350123 to the¦350135 wind¦350143, son¦350128 of¦350128 humanity¦350130, prophesy¦350123 and tell¦350121 the air, ‘The¦350126 master¦350140 Yahweh \add ≈commands\add* this: Breath¦350135, come from¦350142 the four¦350142 \add ≈compass points\add*, and¦350146 breathe¦350146 into these¦350148 who've been killed¦350147, so¦350149 they'll \add ≈come to life¦350149\add*.’ ”
\p
\v 10 \add ≈So¦350151\add* I prophesied¦350151 just¦350152 like¦350152 I was commanded¦350153. Then breath¦350156 came into them¦350155 and¦350151 they \add ≈came to life¦350157\add*. Then they stood¦350158 on¦350159 their¦350161 feet¦350161—a very¦350164 large¦350163 army¦350162.
\p
\v 11 Then Yahweh \add ≈informed\add* me¦350170, “Son¦350171 of¦350171 humanity¦350173, these¦350175 bones are¦350176 the¦350178 entire¦350176 \add ≈Israeli¦350178 population\add*. Listen, they're saying¦350182, ‘Our¦350184 bones have¦350183 dried¦350183 up¦350183 and¦350185 our¦350186 hope¦350186 is gone. We've been¦350187 cut¦350187 off¦350187.’
\v 12 Therefore prophesy¦350191 and¦350192 tell¦350192 them¦350193, ‘The¦350213 master¦350197 Yahweh¦350197 says¦350196 this: Listen, I'll open¦350201 your graves¦350204 and lift you, my¦350197 people¦350208, out from¦350207 them, then I'll bring¦350209 you back to¦350201 Yisrael¦350214.
\v 13 Then¦350226, my¦350229 people¦350229, when¦350222 I open¦350222 your graves¦350225 and¦350226 bring¦350226 you out of¦350225 them, you'll know¦350217 that¦350218 I am¦350221 Yahweh¦350221.
\v 14 I'll place¦350235 my¦350232 spirit¦350232 within you so you'll live¦350234, and I'll cause you to rest in¦350233 your land¦350239 when you know¦350240 that¦350241 I am Yahweh¦350249. I declare it, and I will¦350246 do¦350246 it. That¦350241 is Yahweh's¦350244 declaration¦350247.’ ”
\s1 The two sticks indicating unity of Yisrael and Yehudah
\rem /s1 One Nation Under One King; The Two Sticks; Reunion of Israel and Judah; Judah and Israel in One Kingdom
\p
\v 15 Then Yahweh¦350255 \add ≈gave\add* me¦350256 \add another\add* message¦350253:
\v 16 “\add ≈So¦350259 now\add*, son¦350260 of¦350260 humanity¦350262, take¦350263 a stick for¦350265 yourself¦350265 and¦350268 write¦350268 on¦350269 it¦350269, ‘For¦350270 Yehudah¦350270 and for all their associated people.’ Then¦350259 take¦350275 another stick and¦350278 write¦350278 on¦350279 it¦350279, ‘For¦350280 \add Yisrael\add* (\add represented by\add* Yosef¦350280 \add !(Joseph¦350280)\add*, the¦350281 branch of¦350281 Efrayim¦350282), and¦350283 for all¦350283 their associated people.’
\v 17 Then¦350290 hold both of¦350297 them¦350291 together so that they¦350299 \add ≈seem like\add* one¦350292 stick¦350297 in¦350301 your¦350301 hand¦350301.
\v 18 When¦350303 your¦350307 people¦350307 \add ≈ask you and¦350303 insist\add*, ‘Aren't you going to¦350312 tell¦350311 us¦350312 what¦350313 these¦350315 props of¦350306 yours mean?’
\v 19 then tell¦350322 them¦350319, ‘The¦350330 master¦350323 Yahweh¦350323 says¦350322 this: Look, I'm¦350326 taking¦350327 Yosef's¦350331 branch that's¦350332 in¦350333 Efrayim's¦350335 hand along with¦350333 the¦350336 tribes¦350336 of¦350333 Yisrael¦350337 his¦350338 companions¦350338, and¦350340 joining it¦350342 to¦350319 Yehudah¦350346's branch, so¦350320 that¦350332 they'll make¦350347 one¦350349 branch, and¦350350 they'll become one¦350351 in¦350352 my¦350352 hand.’
\p
\v 20 Hold the¦350355 branches in¦350360 your¦350360 hand¦350360 that¦350356 you¦350358 wrote¦350358 on¦350360 \add ≈while they¦350354 watched\add*.
\v 21 Tell \add @the¦350364 people¦350364\add*, ‘The¦350375 master¦350368 Yahweh¦350368 says¦350367 this: Look, I'm¦350371 about¦350372 to¦350372 take¦350372 the Israeli¦350375 people¦350375 out from¦350377 the¦350378 nations¦350378 where¦350379 they¦350380 went¦350380. I'll¦350383 gather¦350383 them¦350384 from¦350385 the surrounding lands¦350390 and¦350363 bring¦350386 them¦350387 \add back\add* to¦350388 their¦350390 land¦350390.
\v 22 I'll¦350392 \add ≈unite them¦350393 as a¦350394 single¦350395\add* nation¦350394 in¦350397 the land¦350396, on¦350397 the¦350397 mountains¦350397 of¦350397 Yisrael¦350398, and¦350399 there'll be one¦350400 king as king over all¦350402 of them¦350402, and¦350404 they'll no longer be two¦350409 nations¦350410—they'll no longer be¦350412 divided¦350412 into¦350414 two¦350414 kingdoms¦350415.
\v 23 Then¦350418 they'll no longer defile¦350419 themselves¦350419 with their idols¦350421, with their¦350421 disgusting things¦350422, or with any of their other sins¦350430. I'll save¦350425 them¦350426 from¦350427 all¦350427 of¦350428 their¦350428 faithless actions\f + \fr 37:23 \ft The Hebrew text has ‘living places’ rather than ‘faithless actions’ (from the Septuagint), but it's difficult to make sense of the Hebrew.\f* with which¦350429 they've¦350430 sinned¦350430, and¦350432 I'll purify¦350432 them¦350433 so they'll be¦350434 my people¦350437 and¦350438 I'll be their god¦350441.
\v 24 My¦350443 servant¦350443 David¦350444 will¦350445 be¦350445 king¦350445 over¦350446 them¦350446, \add ≈so\add* there'll be one¦350448 shepherd¦350447 over them all¦350450, and¦350451 they'll¦350452 \add ≈follow\add* my instructions¦350453 and keep¦350454 my regulations¦350453 and¦350455 obey them¦350456.\x + \xo 37:24: \xt Eze 34:24.\x*
\v 25 They'll live in the¦350461 land¦350461 that¦350462 I've given¦350463 to¦350464 my servant Yakov¦350465 \add !(Jacob¦350465,\add* \add also called Yisrael/Israel)\add*, where your ancestors¦350470 had stayed¦350467. They'll live in¦350469 it¦350469 forever¦350484—they, their children¦350474, and¦350475 their¦350476 grandchildren, and¦350480 my servant David¦350480 will¦350482 be¦350482 their \add ≈permanent¦350479\add* leader¦350482.
\v 26 I'll establish a peace¦350489 treaty with them—a never-ending agreement¦350488 with them¦350493. I'll establish them¦350494 and¦350495 multiply¦350495 them¦350496 and¦350497 put¦350497 my¦350500 sacred place¦350497 among¦350501 them¦350501 forever¦350502.
\v 27 My¦350505 residence will¦350507 be with¦350506 them¦350506—I'll¦350507 be¦350507 their god¦350509, and¦350504 they'll¦350511 be my¦350505 people¦350514.\x + \xo 37:27: \xt 2Cor 6:16; Rev 21:3.\x*
\v 28 Then¦350516 the¦350517 \add other\add* nations¦350517 will¦350516 know¦350516 that¦350518 I¦350519 am¦350521 Yahweh¦350520 who sets Yisrael¦350524 apart, when¦350525 my¦350526 sacred place is¦350525 \add ≈permanently\add* among¦350527 them¦350527.’ ”
\c 38
\ms1 The defeat of all of Yisrael's opponents
\mr (38:1–39:29)
\s1 Invasion by Gog and his army
\rem /s1 Gog as the Instrument of God; A Message for Gog; A Prophecy Against Gog; Invasion by Gog
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦350534 \add ≈gave\add* me¦350535 \add another\add* message¦350532:
\v 2 “Son¦350538 of¦350538 humanity¦350540, \add ≈look\add* toward the¦350546 land¦350546 of¦350546 Magog¦350547 \add ?where King\add* Gog¦350545 is the main leader¦350548 of Meshek¦350550 and¦350551 Tuval¦350551, and¦350552 prophesy¦350552 against¦350543 him¦350553.\x + \xo 38:2: \xt Rev 20:8.\x*
\v 3 Tell¦350555 him that the¦350563 master¦350558 Yahweh¦350558 says¦350557 this: Listen, I'm¦350560 against¦350561 you¦350561, Gog¦350562, leader¦350563 of¦350563 Meshek¦350565 and¦350566 Tuval¦350566,
\v 4 \add ≈so\add* I'll turn¦350568 you¦350568 around¦350568 and¦350569 put¦350569 hooks¦350570 into your jaws¦350571. Then¦350568 I'll bring¦350572 you out¦350572 with all¦350577 your army¦350579, horses¦350580, and¦350581 horsemen¦350581, all of them dressed¦350582 in¦350571 full armour—a huge¦350586 group¦350585 with large¦350586 and¦350588 small shields¦350588, all of them holding swords¦350590.
\v 5 Persia, \add Ethiopia\add* (Kush¦350594), and¦350595 Libya are with¦350596 them, all¦350597 of them with shields¦350598 and¦350599 helmets¦350599,
\v 6 \add as well as\add* Gomer¦350601 and¦350602 all¦350602 its troops, and Beyt-Togarmah¦350606, from the¦350607 far parts¦350607 of¦350605 the¦350608 north¦350608, and¦350609 all¦350611 its troops. Many¦350615 people¦350614 groups are¦350616 with¦350616 you¦350616.
\v 7 \add Tell Gog to\add* \add ≈get¦350627 ready¦350619 as commander, and to assemble¦350624 and prepare¦350618 his troops\add*.
\v 8 You'll be \add ≈summoned many days¦350631 later\add*, then after some years¦350635 you'll¦350633 go¦350636 to¦350638 a land¦350640 that's recovered from war and \add ≈where the people have come¦350636 back from¦350643 many nations\add*—gathered¦350644 back to Yisrael's¦350649 mountains¦350648 that¦350650 had¦350652 continuously¦350654 been¦350657 a ruin. But¦350655 the land's¦350640 people will¦350658 \add indeed\add* be brought¦350657 out¦350657 of¦350635 the nations, and they'll¦350658 all¦350660 live¦350658 \add there\add* safely \add again\add*.
\v 9 Then¦350662 you'll go¦350664 \add ≈in like a storm¦350663 with¦350675 your¦350672 large army\add*—you'll all¦350670 be¦350668 like a cloud¦350665 covering¦350666 the¦350667 land¦350667.
\p
\v 10 The¦350681 master¦350680 Yahweh¦350680 says¦350679 this: \add But\add* plans will¦350686 \add start to\add* form in¦350684 your¦350690 heart¦350690 on¦350688 that¦350685 day¦350684 and¦350691 you'll¦350691 devise¦350691 wicked¦350693 schemes.
\v 11 Then¦350695 you'll¦350695 \add ≈think\add*, ‘I'll¦350696 \add take my army\add* up¦350696 onto the open ground¦350699—\add ≈we'll attack\add* the people living quietly \add ≈and peacefully¦350702\add*—all of¦350699 them¦350705 living where there¦350711 are¦350706 no walls¦350708 or barriers, and no city gates¦350710.
\v 12 I'll capture¦350716 booty and steal plunder¦350715 \add ≈and¦350716 use my forces\add* against those ruins¦350722 that¦350727 have¦350727 been¦350727 newly inhabited¦350723, and¦350724 against those people¦350726 who've returned from¦350728 the nations¦350728—people who are gaining¦350729 livestock¦350730 and¦350731 property¦350731, and who¦350732 are living¦350732 at¦350733 the¦350735 centre¦350735 of¦350735 the¦350736 world¦350736.’
\v 13 \add People from\add* Sheva and¦350739 Dedan¦350739, and¦350740 traders¦350740 from Tarshish¦350741 and¦350742 its¦350744 villages¦350744 will¦350745 \add ≈ask¦350745\add* you, ‘Have you come¦350750 to¦350751 plunder? Have¦350753 you¦350753 assembled¦350753 your¦350754 armies to take away spoil¦350752, to¦350755 carry¦350755 off gold¦350758 and silver¦350757, to¦350759 take¦350759 their livestock¦350760 and¦350761 property¦350761 and to haul away plenty of¦350740 plunder?’
\p
\v 14 Therefore, son¦350769 of¦350769 humanity¦350771, prophesy¦350768 and¦350772 tell¦350772 Gog¦350773 that the¦350780 master¦350776 Yahweh¦350776 says¦350775 this: On that day¦350780, when¦350782 my¦350783 people¦350783 Yisrael¦350784 are¦350778 living¦350782 securely¦350785\add ≈—but¦350772 you¦350786 won't¦350778 take notice of that—\add*
\v 15 you'll¦350788 come¦350788 from¦350789 your¦350789 place¦350789 far away in the¦350790 north¦350791 with¦350795 a large¦350800 army¦350801—all of¦350796 them¦350798 riding¦350796 on horses¦350797, \add yes,\add* \add ≈a very numerous force\add*.
\v 16 Then¦350804 you'll¦350804 attack my \add ≈Israeli people¦350807\add* like¦350809 a cloud¦350809 that covers¦350810 the¦350811 land¦350811. I'll¦350815 send you against my land \add ≈near the end¦350812 of¦350818 the era\add*, so¦350819 that the¦350821 nations¦350821 might know¦350820 me¦350822 when¦350823 I show¦350823 myself¦350823 through you, Gog¦350826—\add ≈they'll see¦350820 with¦350823 their¦350825 own eyes¦350825 that I always demand what's right\add*.
\rem /s1 Judgment on Gog
\v 17 The¦350842 master¦350832 Yahweh¦350832 says¦350831 this: Aren't you¦350834 the one that I spoke¦350839 about¦350842 in the past \add ≈through¦350842\add* my¦350832 servants¦350843, the¦350844 Israeli¦350844 prophets¦350844 who¦350846 prophesied¦350846 for years¦350849 in their own times, that I would bring¦350850 you¦350851 against¦350852 them¦350852?
\s1 Yahweh's punishment of Gog
\rem /s1 God's Punishment of Gog
\p
\v 18 This is¦350855 the¦350857 master¦350867 Yahweh's¦350868 declaration¦350866: When Gog¦350861 attacks Yisrael¦350865, my¦350867 fury¦350870 will¦350869 mount up \add ≈into a rage¦350870\add*.
\v 19 In¦350873 my zeal and¦350873 in¦350874 the¦350874 fire¦350874 of¦350874 my¦350876 anger¦350876, I¦350877 declare that on¦350873 that day¦350882 there'll be¦350884 a terrible¦350876 earthquake¦350885 in Yisrael¦350889,
\v 20 and¦350891 the¦350893 fish¦350893 in the¦350894 sea¦350894 and¦350895 the birds¦350895 in the¦350896 skies¦350896, the¦350897 wild animals¦350897 in the¦350898 countryside¦350898 including¦350895 all¦350899 the creatures that¦350908 crawl on the earth, and every person who's on the surface¦350911 of¦350911 the¦350912 land¦350920 will tremble¦350891 in front¦350892 of¦350892 me¦350892. The¦350914 mountains¦350914 will be¦350913 thrown¦350913 down¦350913 and¦350915 the¦350916 cliffs¦350916 will¦350921 fall¦350921, until every wall¦350919 falls to¦350920 the ground¦350920.
\v 21 I'll¦350923 summon¦350923 \add ≈an army\add* against \add @Gog¦350923\add* on¦350934 all¦350925 my¦350927 mountains¦350927. Every¦350925 man's sword¦350928 will¦350935 be¦350935 against his¦350934 brother¦350934. That's the¦350929 master¦350930 Yahweh's¦350931 declaration¦350929.
\v 22 Then¦350937 I'll \add ≈punish\add* \add @Gog¦350937\add* with¦350938 \add ≈deadly diseases\add* and¦350940 bloodshed¦350940, as well as overwhelming rain and hailstones and burning¦350945 sulfur¦350946 that I'll rain¦350947 down¦350947 on¦350939 him¦350948 and¦350949 his¦350951 troops¦350951 and¦350952 the many¦350955 nations¦350954 that¦350956 \add ≈joined\add* with¦350957 him¦350957.
\v 23 \add Yes,\add* I'll display¦350959 my greatness¦350959 and¦350960 \add ≈purity¦350960\add*, and¦350961 I'll make¦350961 myself¦350961 known¦350961 to¦350962 \add &those¦350962\add* many¦350964 nations¦350963, \add ≈so\add* they'll¦350965 know¦350965 that¦350966 I am¦350969 Yahweh¦350969.
\c 39
\s1 The defeat of Gog
\rem /s1 The Defeat of Gog; The Slaughter of Gog's Armies; Gog's Armies Destroyed
\p
\v 1 “Now, son¦350973 of¦350973 humanity¦350975, prophesy¦350976 against Gog¦350979 and¦350980 say¦350980 that the¦350988 master¦350983 Yahweh¦350983 says¦350982 this: Listen, I'm¦350985 against¦350986 you¦350986, Gog¦350987, leader¦350988 of Meshek¦350990 and¦350991 Tuval¦350991.
\v 2 I'll turn¦350993 you¦350993 around¦350993 and¦350994 drag you¦350994 along¦350994—I'll bring¦350995 you¦350995 from¦350996 the¦350996 far north¦350997 and take you up¦350995 to Yisrael's¦351002 mountains¦351001,
\v 3 Then¦351004 I'll¦351011 knock your bow¦351005 out of your left¦351007 hand and¦351004 make¦351011 the¦351006 arrows¦351008 fall¦351011 out of your right¦351010 hand.
\v 4 You¦351017 and¦351019 all¦351019 your¦351021 troops¦351021 and¦351022 soldiers who are¦351024 with¦351024 you will¦351024 \add ≈die\add* on¦351013 Yisrael's¦351016 mountains¦351015. I'll¦351032 give¦351032 you to¦351025 the birds¦351025 of¦351030 prey¦351025 and¦351030 the¦351030 wild animals¦351030 in the¦351031 countryside¦351031 for¦351033 food¦351033.
\v 5 You'll die \add ≈there\add* in the countryside¦351038, because¦351040 I¦351041 myself declare it. That's the¦351043 master¦351044 Yahweh's¦351045 declaration¦351043.
\v 6 Then¦351047 I'll¦351047 send¦351047 fire¦351049 out onto Magog¦351050 and on¦351050 those¦351051 living¦351051 in safety¦351053 in the¦351052 \add ≈coastal¦351052 regions\add*, and then¦351047 they'll¦351054 know¦351054 that¦351055 I¦351057 am¦351058 Yahweh¦351058.
\v 7 I'll make¦351064 my holy name known¦351064 among my people¦351066 Yisrael, and¦351060 I'll no longer allow¦351070 my holy name to be¦351070 profaned¦351070—the nations¦351078 will¦351077 know¦351077 that¦351079 I¦351064 am¦351083 Yahweh¦351082, the holy¦351083 One in¦351084 Yisrael¦351084.
\p
\v 8 Listen, the¦351093 day¦351093 is¦351087 coming¦351087, and¦351088 \add @all¦351094 that¦351094\add* will¦351088 take place. That's the¦351089 master¦351090 Yahweh's¦351091 declaration¦351089.
\v 9 The¦351098 people¦351098 living¦351098 in¦351104 Yisrael's¦351101 cities¦351100 will¦351097 go¦351097 out¦351097 and¦351102 they'll use \add those\add* weapons¦351104 to kindle¦351102 and¦351103 make fires¦351103 and¦351105 burn them—small shields¦351105, large shields¦351106, bows¦351107, arrows¦351108, the¦351100 clubs¦351109 and¦351111 spears¦351111—they'll make fires with¦351104 them¦351113 for seven¦351115 years¦351116.
\v 10 They won't¦351118 \add need to\add* gather firewood¦351121 from¦351122 the¦351124 countryside¦351124 or cut¦351126 down trees from¦351127 the¦351129 forests¦351129, since they'll¦351120 burn the weapons¦351131. They'll take from those \add invaders\add* who wanted to take from them, and¦351118 plunder¦351135 those¦351138 who¦351138 wanted to plunder¦351138 them¦351138. That's¦351142 the¦351143 master¦351144 Yahweh's¦351145 declaration¦351143.”
\s1 Gog's burial
\rem /s1 The Burial of Gog
\p
\v 11 Then \add ≈at¦351149 that¦351150 time\add*, I'll¦351151 make a grave for Gog there in¦351149 Yisrael¦351158—a valley¦351159 for those¦351160 who¦351160 journey to the¦351161 east¦351161 of¦351161 the¦351162 sea¦351162. They'll bury¦351168 Gog there with¦351149 all¦351175 his¦351177 multitudes¦351177, and¦351179 they'll¦351179 call¦351179 it¦351148 the ‘Hamon¦351180-Gog’ \add (or, ‘Gog's horde’)\add* valley. \add @That¦351150 mass¦351150 grave¦351150\add* will¦351151 block¦351163 people¦351168 who want to cross over.
\v 12 It'll¦351186 take seven¦351192 months¦351193 for the Israelis¦351185 to bury¦351184 them¦351184 to make the area clean¦351188—
\v 13 all¦351196 the land's¦351199 people¦351198 will¦351195 bury¦351195 them¦351195. It'll be¦351200 a¦351202 memorable day¦351203 for¦351201 them¦351201 when I'm \add ≈honoured¦351202\add*. That's the master¦351206 Yahweh's¦351207 declaration¦351205.
\v 14 At the end¦351226 of¦351209 the seven¦351227 months¦351229, they'll¦351211 designate men¦351209 to continually¦351210 go through the \add ≈region\add* to find people¦351209 who were travelling through, but¦351209 who died and¦351209 their bodies remained¦351220 \add ≈above the ground¦351213\add*, so that¦351214 they can bury¦351214 them to¦351225 make¦351230 the land¦351224 clean¦351225.
\v 15 As¦351249 those¦351233 men pass¦351232 through the¦351234 land¦351234, when they¦351235 see¦351235 any human¦351237 bone¦351236, they'll¦351232 put a¦351236 marker¦351240 by it, until¦351241 gravediggers come and¦351232 bury¦351244 it in the¦351247 Hamon¦351247-Gog¦351248 valley¦351247.
\v 16 There'll even be¦351255 a city¦351254 there named¦351252 ‘Hamonah¦351255’ \add (which means, ‘horde’ or ‘multitude’)\add*. In that way, they'll¦351256 make the¦351252 land¦351257 clean¦351256 \add again\add*.
\p
\v 17 Now, son¦351261 of¦351261 humanity¦351263, the master¦351268 Yahweh¦351268 says¦351266 this to you: Tell¦351270 all the winged birds¦351271 and¦351275 all¦351275 the¦351277 wild animals¦351277 in the¦351278 countryside¦351278, ‘Gather together and¦351280 come¦351280. Gather¦351281 from¦351282 all around¦351282 to¦351283 the sacrifice¦351285 that I¦351287 myself am¦351288 making for¦351289 you—a large¦351291 sacrifice on¦351292 Yisrael's¦351294 mountains¦351293, so¦351264 that you can eat¦351295 \add human\add* flesh¦351296 and¦351297 drink¦351297 blood¦351298.\x + \xo 39:17-20: \xt Rev 19:17-18.\x*
\v 18 You'll eat¦351302 warriors¦351301' flesh¦351300 and¦351303 drink¦351307 the blood¦351303 of¦351303 the¦351305 \add ≈world's leaders¦351305\add* as if they were rams¦351308, lambs¦351309, goats¦351310, and bulls¦351311 that were all¦351314 fattened¦351312 in Bashan¦351313.
\v 19 Then¦351316 you'll eat¦351316 fat¦351318 until \add you're\add* full \add and\add* drink¦351320 blood¦351321 until \add you're\add* drunk¦351322—that'll be the sacrifice¦351323 that¦351324 I'll¦351326 slaughter for¦351327 you \add birds and animals\add*.
\v 20 You'll be¦351329 satisfied¦351329 at¦351330 my¦351332 table¦351332 with \add #horses¦351333, chariot¦351334 drivers¦351334, warriors¦351335,\add* and¦351329 every¦351336 man¦351338 of¦351338 war¦351339. That's the¦351340 master¦351341 Yahweh's¦351342 declaration¦351340.’
\s1 Yisrael's restoration
\rem /s1 Israel Restored to the Land; The Restoration of Israel
\p
\v 21 I'll \add ≈display¦351344 my¦351347 power\add* among¦351348 the nations¦351348, and¦351349 all¦351350 the nations will¦351344 see¦351349 \add ≈my judgement¦351355 that I'll put into process\add* and \add ≈how¦351356 I'll put that into action¦351356\add* against them¦351364.
\v 22 Then¦351366 from¦351373 that¦351376 \add ≈time\add* onwards¦351377, the¦351367 \add ≈Israeli¦351368 people\add* will¦351366 know¦351366 that¦351369 I¦351370 am¦351371 their¦351372 god¦351372 Yahweh¦351371.
\v 23 The¦351395 nations¦351380 will¦351379 know¦351379 that¦351381 the¦351384 \add ≈Israeli¦351386 people\add* went¦351383 into¦351383 captivity because¦351381 of¦351386 how they¦351389 betrayed me¦351391 with¦351382 their¦351382 \add ≈disobedience\add*, so I¦351392 \add ≈distanced myself\add* from¦351394 them and¦351379 \add ≈handed¦351394 them over¦351394 to¦351394\add* their¦351397 adversaries¦351397 so that they¦351398 all¦351400 \add ≈died in¦351382 the¦351396 battle\add*.
\v 24 When I \add ≈distanced myself\add* from¦351408 them, I \add ≈treated¦351402 them exactly¦351402 as¦351402 their¦351402 defilement¦351402 and¦351402 rebellion¦351402 deserved¦351402\add*.
\rem /s1 Restoration for God's People
\p
\v 25 Therefore the¦351420 master¦351414 Yahweh¦351414 says¦351413 this: Now¦351416 I'll restore Yakov's¦351422 fortunes, and¦351423 I'll have¦351423 compassion¦351423 on¦351423 all¦351424 of¦351426 Yisrael's¦351427 \add ≈descendants\add*, when I¦351428 act with zeal \add ≈to protect my¦351414 pure¦351430 reputation¦351429\add*.
\v 26 Then¦351432 they'll¦351432 bear¦351432 their shame¦351435 and¦351432 all the treason in which¦351441 they¦351442 betrayed me¦351444. They'll forget¦351432 all that¦351441 when¦351445 they¦351445 rest in their land¦351448 in safety¦351449, with¦351444 no one¦351451 to¦351449 terrify¦351451 them
\v 27 \add when\add* I restore them¦351454 from¦351455 the¦351457 people¦351457 groups and¦351458 gather¦351458 them¦351459 from¦351460 their¦351461 enemies¦351461'¦351461 lands¦351460, and¦351462 I show¦351462 myself¦351462 in¦351463 the¦351464 sight¦351464 of¦351464 many¦351466 nations¦351465 \add ≈to¦351464 always do what's right\add*.
\v 28 Then¦351468 they'll¦351468 know¦351468 that¦351469 I am¦351471 Yahweh¦351471 their god¦351472, because¦351473 I sent¦351473 them into¦351473 captivity among the \add other\add* nations, but¦351468 then¦351468 I'll¦351484 gather¦351478 them¦351478 back to¦351479 their \add own\add* land¦351481. I won't¦351482 leave¦351484 any of¦351472 them¦351474 among the¦351477 nations¦351477.
\v 29 I'll¦351491 no longer \add ≈distance myself\add* from¦351494 them¦351494 when I¦351495 pour¦351496 out¦351496 my¦351499 spirit¦351499 on¦351500 the¦351502 \add ≈Israeli¦351502 people\add*. That's the¦351504 master¦351505 Yahweh's¦351506 declaration¦351504.”
\c 40
\ms1 The revelation concerning the coming temple and nation
\mr (40:1–48:35)
