\rem /s1 Ezekiel Is Taken to Jerusalem; The Vision of the New Temple; The new temple; The New Temple Area
\p
\v 1 In¦351509 \add ≈mid-April\add* of the twenty-fifth¦351509 year¦351511 of¦351512 our¦351512 captivity (the fourteenth year after¦351520 \add @Yerushalem¦351512\add* was¦351522 captured), Yahweh¦351532 \add ≈used his power to take\add* me¦351529 there¦351535,
\v 2 \add yes,\add* God¦351538 took¦351539 me¦351539 to¦351540 Yisrael¦351543 in¦351537 visions¦351537. He¦351544 put¦351544 me¦351544 on¦351550 a very¦351549 high¦351548 mountain¦351547 \add where\add* there seemed to be¦351550 city¦351553 buildings towards the¦351551 south¦351554,\x + \xo 40:2: \xt Rev 21:10.\x*
\v 3 and¦351556 he¦351556 took¦351556 me¦351557 there. Then¦351556 wow, there was a man¦351561 standing¦351572 in¦351573 the¦351563 city gateway¦351573 who \add ≈looked like¦351563\add* bronze¦351564! \add ≈He¦351559 was¦351563 holding\add* a linen¦351567 cord¦351565 and¦351569 a measuring¦351570 rod.\x + \xo 40:3: \xt Rev 11:1; 21:15.\x*
\p
\v 4 The¦351577 man¦351577 told¦351598 me¦351576, “Son¦351578 of¦351578 humanity¦351580, look with¦351582 your eyes¦351582 and¦351583 listen¦351584 with your ears¦351583, and¦351585 fix¦351585 your mind¦351586 on¦351582 everything¦351587 that¦351588 I'm¦351590 revealing to¦351591 you¦351592, because¦351593 you were¦351596 brought¦351596 here so¦351594 I could reveal them to¦351595 you. Report everything you see¦351606 \add here\add* to¦351607 the¦351607 \add ≈Israeli¦351607 people¦351580\add*.”
\s1 The eastern gateway
\rem /s1 The East Gateway; The East Gate to the Outer Court; The East Gate
\p
\v 5 There was a wall surrounding the¦351612 temple¦351613 area. The¦351617 measuring rod in¦351617 the¦351618 man's¦351618 hand¦351617 was¦351621 \add ≈just over three metres¦351623 long\add*. (It was six¦351621 long cubits—each¦351614 long cubit was a cubit long plus¦351617 a handbreadth¦351625.) \add ≈So¦351610\add* he¦351626 measured¦351626 the wall, and it was one¦351632 measuring rod thick and¦351633 one high¦351633.\x + \xo 40:5–42:20: \xt 1Ki 6:1-38; 2Ch 3:1-9.\x*
\v 6 Then¦351637 he¦351637 went¦351637 to¦351638 the¦351640 temple gate¦351640 that¦351641 faced¦351642 east¦351644. He¦351645 went up its¦351646 steps¦351646 and¦351637 measured¦351648 the gate's¦351653 threshold¦351658—one rod across.
\v 7 The guard chambers¦351672 were each one rod \add ≈long¦351667 and¦351668 deep, and¦351671 just under three metres¦351674 wide¦351670\add*. The temple gate¦351676 threshold¦351675 by¦351677 the¦351678 temple porch¦351678 was one¦351682 rod across.
\v 8 He¦351684 measured¦351684 the¦351687 porch¦351687 inside¦351689 the gate¦351688 and¦351684 it was one¦351691 rod long,
\v 9 and¦351693 the¦351696 porch¦351696 over the¦351697 gate¦351697 was one rod deep. The¦351704 doorposts were \add each\add* a metre wide. (This was the porch¦351704 at the¦351705 gate¦351705 facing the¦351706 temple¦351706.)
\v 10 There were three¦351712 guard chambers¦351708 on either side of¦351708 the east¦351711 gate¦351709, and each of¦351710 them \add ≈was the¦351711 same size\add*, and¦351714 the¦351718 walls that separated them¦351718 \add ≈were the same size\add*.
\p
\v 11 Then¦351725 the man measured¦351725 the¦351728 width¦351728 of¦351728 the¦351729 gateway entrance¦351729 \add ≈and it was five metres\add*, and the length¦351734 of¦351734 the¦351735 gateway entrance \add ≈was almost seven metres\add*.
\v 12 He measured the wall that \add ≈ran along\add* the front¦351741 of¦351741 the¦351742 chambers¦351742 at half a metre high. The¦351750 chambers¦351750 measured three metres¦351753 on each side.
\v 13 Then¦351759 he¦351759 measured¦351759 the¦351762 gateway¦351762 from¦351763 the¦351763 roof¦351763 of one chamber to that of the next chamber, \add ≈and¦351759 it was thirteen metres¦351769\add* from the entrance¦351770 of the first chamber to that of the second.
\v 14 Then¦351774 he¦351774 measured the wall that went between the guard chambers, \add ≈and¦351774 it¦351774 was over thirty metres long\add* as far as the gate's¦351784 porch.
\v 15 The¦351790 entrance¦351792 from the¦351796 front¦351796 of the gate to¦351796 the¦351797 other end of¦351797 the¦351798 gate's¦351798 porch¦351797 was twenty-seven metres.
\v 16 There were closed¦351804 windows facing the¦351807 chambers¦351807 and¦351808 toward their¦351809 pillars¦351824 within¦351810 the gates¦351811 all around, and¦351815 likewise for the porches¦351816. There were windows¦351817 all around the inside¦351821, and each¦351812 of the door jambs was¦351818 decorated with \add carvings of\add* palm¦351825 trees¦351825.
\s1 The temple courtyard
