\p
\v 17 Then¦351827 the man brought¦351827 me¦351827 to¦351828 the outer¦351831 courtyard of the temple. Look¦351832, there were rooms, and¦351827 the courtyard \add ≈was paved\add*, with thirty¦351840 rooms¦351841 next to¦351842 the¦351844 pavement¦351844.
\v 18 The¦351846 pavement¦351846 \add ≈reached\add* to¦351847 the side¦351849 of¦351849 the gates, and¦351846 its width was¦351847 the same as the¦351850 gates¦351850' length¦351852. That was the lower¦351855 pavement.
\v 19 Then¦351857 the man measured¦351857 the¦351858 distance from¦351859 the front of the lower¦351861 gate to¦351862 the¦351862 front¦351862 of the inner¦351864 gate: it was \add ≈just over fifty metres\add* on the¦351868 eastern¦351868 side, and¦351869 the same on the northern¦351869 side.
\s1 The northern gateway
