\p
\v 20 Then¦351871 he¦351878 measured¦351878 the length¦351879 and¦351871 width¦351880 of the gate¦351871 that¦351872 was¦351874 at the northern¦351875 \add end\add* of¦351876 the¦351877 outer¦351877 courtyard¦351876.
\v 21 There were three¦351884 chambers¦351882 on¦351902 each side of¦351888 that gate, and¦351890 the gate¦351894 with¦351902 its¦351888 porch¦351890 measured¦351893 the same as the main gate: \add ≈twenty-seven¦351901 metres long¦351898 and¦351899 thirteen metres wide¦351899\add*.
\v 22 Its¦351904 windows¦351904, porch¦351906, chambers, and¦351908 its¦351908 palm¦351908 trees¦351908 matched the¦351910 eastern¦351915 gate¦351911. Seven¦351917 steps¦351916 went¦351918 up¦351918 to it¦351920 and¦351921 to its¦351921 porch.
\v 23 There was a gate¦351925 to¦351926 the inner¦351927 courtyard¦351926 in front¦351928 of the¦351929 northern¦351930 gate, just as there was at the eastern¦351931 gate. The¦351927 man measured¦351932 from¦351933 one gate to the other gate, \add ≈and¦351925 it was¦351928 fifty-four metres\add*.
\s1 The southern gateway
