\p
\v 24 Next¦351943 the man took¦351940 me¦351940 to the gateway¦351945 at the southern¦351942 entrance¦351945, and¦351948 its¦351949 walls and¦351951 porch¦351951 measured¦351948 the same as the other outer gates¦351945.
\v 25 There were closed windows¦351956 in the gateway and¦351958 its¦351958 porch just \add ≈like¦351963 the¦351963 other gates\add*. The¦351964 southern gate with its porch \add ≈was¦351965 twenty-seven¦351970 metres long¦351967 and¦351968 thirteen metres wide¦351968\add*.
\v 26 There were¦351973 seven¦351974 steps¦351973 up to¦351981 the gate and its¦351975 porch¦351977, and¦351980 \add carvings of\add* palm¦351980 trees¦351980 on the walls on each side.
\v 27 There was a gate¦351991 to¦351992 the¦351993 inner¦351993 courtyard¦351992 on the southern¦351995 side, and¦351996 the man measured¦351996 fifty-four metres¦352004 from¦351997 that gate¦351997 to¦351998 the¦352000 gate¦352000 at the southern¦352002 entrance.
\s1 The gateways to the inner courtyard
